has 0. So 0 + 0 = 0. Then ten millions place: 5 (from first number) and 6 (from second number). 5 + 6 = 11. Oh, here's a carry-over. So we write down 1 and carry over 1 to the next higher place, which is the hundred millions place..\n\nThen the hundred millions place: 7 (from first number) + 3 (from second number) plus the carried-over 1. 7 + 3 is 10, plus 1 is 11. So here, we write down 1 and carry over another 1. But since there are no higher places left, that carry-over would create a new digit at the beginning. .\n\nPutting all the digits together with the carries:.\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\nOnes: 1 + 8 = 9.\n\nTens: 2 + 4 = 6.\n\nHundreds: 6 + 3 = 9.\n\nThousands: 7 + 2 = 9.\n\nTen thousands: 8 + 0 = 8.\n\nHundred thousands: 2 + 1 = 3.\n\nMillions: 0 + 0 = 0 (but wait, maybe I got the places mixed up here. Let me check again.).\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the place alignment. Let me write both numbers properly:.\n\nFirst number: 750,287,621.\n\nBreakdown:.\n- 7 (hundred millions).\n- 5 (ten millions).\n- 0 (millions).\n- 2 (hundred thousands).\n- 8 (ten thousands).\n- 7 (thousands).\n- 6 (hundreds).\n- 2 (tens).\n- 1 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 360,102,348.\n\nBreakdown:.\n- 3 (hundred millions).\n- 6 (ten millions).\n- 0 (millions).\n- 1 (hundred thousands).\n- 0 (ten thousands).\n- 2 (thousands).\n- 3 (hundreds).\n- 4 (tens).\n- 8 (ones).\n\nSo when adding, the places from right to left:.\n\nOnes: 1 +8 =9.\n\nTens: 2 +4=6.\n\nHundreds:6 +3=9.\n\nThousands:7 +2=9.\n\nTen thousands:8 +0=8.\n\nHundred thousands:2 +1=3.\n\nMillions:0 +0=0.\n\nTen millions:5 +6=11 (so we put 1 here, carry over 1).\n\nHundred millions:7 +3=10, plus the carried 1 makes 11 (so put 1 here, carry over 1).\n\nNow, since we're at the highest place (hundred millions), the carry-over 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning: 1 (billions place). Wait, but 750 million plus 360 million is 1,110 million</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
