d). 9 + 1 = 10. So we write 0 here and carry over 1..\n\nHundred thousands place: 1 (from first) + 5 (from second) plus the carryover 1. That's 1 + 5 + 1 = 7. So 7 here, no carry-over..\n\nMillions place: 4 (from first) + 3 (from second). 4 + 3 = 7. So 7 here..\n\nTen millions place: 2 (from first) + 0 (from second). That's 2 + 0 = 2..\n\nHundred millions place: 8 (from first) + 2 (from second). 8 + 2 = 10. So we write 0 here and carry over 1 to the billions place..\n\nWait, but since these are 9-digit numbers, the next place is billions. So the carryover 1 becomes the billions digit. So putting it all together:.\n\nThe sum would be 1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands?), wait let me check again..\n\nWait, let's go through each step carefully:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 2 + 1 = 3 → ones digit 3..\n\nTens: 2 + 9 = 11 → tens digit 1, carryover 1..\n\nHundreds: 6 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 8 → hundreds digit 8..\n\nThousands: 0 + 4 = 4 → thousands digit 4..\n\nTen thousands: 9 + 1 = 10 → ten thousands digit 0, carryover 1..\n\nHundred thousands: 1 + 5 + 1 = 7 → hundred thousands digit 7..\n\nMillions: 4 + 3 = 7 → millions digit 7..\n\nTen millions: 2 + 0 = 2 → ten millions digit 2..\n\nHundred millions: 8 + 2 = 10 → hundred millions digit 0, carryover 1 to billions..\n\nSo the total sum would be 1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands?), wait wait, wait. Wait, after hundred thousands, we have ten thousands, thousands, etc. Wait, let me structure each digit position properly..\n\nLet me write each digit position step by step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones place: 2 + 1 = 3. Sum digit: 3. Carryover: 0..\n\n2. Tens place: 2 + 9 = 11. Sum digit: 1. Carryover: 1..\n\n3. Hundreds place: 6 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 8. Sum digit:8. Carryover:0..\n\n4. Thousands place: 0 + 4 =4. Sum digit:4. Carryover:0..\n\n5. Ten thousands place:9 +1=10. Sum digit:0. Carryover:1..\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:1 +5 +1=7. Sum digit:7. Carryover:0..\n\n7. Millions place:4 +3=7. Sum digit:7. Carryover:0..\n\n8. Ten millions place:2 +0=2. Sum digit:2. Carryover:0..\n\n9. Hundred millions place:8 +2=10. Sum digit:0. Carryover:1..\n\n10. Billions place: carryover 1. Sum digit:1..\n\nSo putting all the digits together from left to right (highest to lowest place):.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:0.\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nHundred thousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:0.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nTens:1.\n\nOnes:3.\n\nWait, but the order is billions, hundred millions, ten millions, millions, hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands, hundreds, tens, ones</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]  1%|1         | 5/500 [00:12<19:58,  2.42s/it]  1%|1         | 6/500 [00:14<20:14,  2.46s/it]
