over becomes a new digit at the beginning. So the final sum starts with 1, then 6..\n\nPutting all the digits together: 1,6 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 7 (ones). Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits..\n\nWait, let me recheck each place step by step to avoid mistakes. Starting from ones:.\n\nOnes: 6 +1=7. Correct..\n\nTens:5+7=12, write 2, carry 1..\n\nHundreds:4+8=12 +1=13, write 3, carry1..\n\nThousands:2+3=5 +1=6. Correct..\n\nTen thousands:0+6=6. Correct..\n\nHundred thousands:0+8=8. Correct..\n\nMillions:6+4=10, write 0, carry1..\n\nTen millions:9+6=15 +1=16, write6, carry1..\n\nHundred millions:7+8=15 +1=16, write6, carry1. Since there are no higher digits, that carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the front</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
