e positions..\n\nWait, maybe the carryover from each step is added to the next higher position. So when adding position3 (hundreds), the sum is 9+1=10. So we write 0 and carryover1. Then when moving to position4 (thousands), which is 1 (from first number) +9 (from second number) plus carryover1. So 1+9+1=11. So digit1, carryover1..\n\nThen position5 (ten-thousands):6 +7 +1=14. So digit4, carryover1..\n\nPosition6 (hundred-thousands):2 +5 +1=8. Digit8, carryover0..\n\nPosition7 (millions):0 +6 +0=6. Digit6, carryover0..\n\nPosition8 (ten-millions):6 +1 +0=7. Digit7, carryover0..\n\nPosition9 (hundred-millions):1 +6 +0=7. Digit7..\n\nSo compiling all digits from position9 to position1:.\n\n7 (hundred-millions),7 (ten-millions),6 (millions),8 (hundred-thousands),4 (ten-thousands),1 (thousands),0 (hundreds),7 (tens),2 (ones)..\n\nWait, but let's check:.\n\nWait the digits after each position:.\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nPosition2:7.\n\nPosition3:0.\n\nPosition4:1 (since 1+9+1=11, so 1 here).\n\nPosition5:4 (6+7+1=14, so 4 here with carry 1).\n\nPosition6:8 (2+5+1=8).\n\nPosition7:6 (0+6=6).\n\nPosition8:7 (6+1=7).\n\nPosition9:7 (1+6=7).\n\nSo the number would be 7 (9th position) 7 (8th) 6 (7th) 8 (6th) 4 (5th) 1 (4th) 0 (3rd) 7 (2nd) 2 (1st)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]  3%|3         | 15/500 [01:32<36:04,  4.46s/it]  3%|3         | 16/500 [01:34<31:19,  3.88s/it]
