nds:2.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nTens:2.\n\nOnes:9.\n\nSo adding:.\n\nHundred millions:5 +3 =8, but earlier we had a carryover of 1 from the ten millions place addition. Wait, no. Wait, let's re-examine:.\n\nWait, when adding digit by digit from right to left (ones to the left), the carry propagates to the next left digit. So let's redo the addition step by step properly..\n\nStarting with the ones place:.\n\nPosition1 (ones):7 +9 =16. Write 6, carry 1..\n\nPosition2 (tens):9 +2 =11 +1 (carry) =12. Write 2, carry 1..\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):9 +7 =16 +1 =17. Write7, carry1..\n\nPosition4 (thousands):5 +2 =7 +1 =8. Write8, no carry..\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):2 +2 =4. Write4..\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):5 +6 =11. Write1, carry1..\n\nPosition7 (millions):1 +7 =8 +1 =9. Write9..\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):9 +9 =18. Write8, carry1..\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):5 +3 =8 +1 (carry) =9. Write9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]  3%|3         | 17/500 [01:37<28:54,  3.59s/it]
