 2 6 8 5 4 0 2 0 7.\n        --------------------.\n\nStarting from the ones digit (rightmost):.\n\n3 +7 =10 → 0, carryover 1..\n\nNext, tens place: 9 +0 =9 +1 =10 → 0, carryover 1..\n\nHundreds place: 1 +2 =3 +1 =4 → 4, no carryover..\n\nThousands place:7 +0 =7 → 7..\n\nTen thousands place:2 +4 =6 →6..\n\nHundred thousands place:4 +5 =9 →9..\n\nMillions place:9 +8 =17 →7, carryover 1..\n\nTen millions place:1 +6 =7 +1=8 →8..\n\nHundred millions place:1 +2 =3 →3..\n\nWait, let me check again step by step..\n\nLet me list each digit position clearly:.\n\nPositions (from right to left, ones to hundred millions):.\n\n1. Ones: 3 +7 =10 →0, carry 1..\n\n2. Tens:9 +0=9 +1=10 →0, carry 1..\n\n3. Hundreds:1 +2=3 +1=4 →4, carry 0..\n\n4. Thousands:7 +0=7 →7, carry 0..\n\n5. Ten thousands:2 +4=6 →6, carry 0..\n\n6. Hundred thousands:4 +5=9 →9, carry 0..\n\n7. Millions:9 +8=17 →7, carry 1..\n\n8. Ten millions:1 +6=7 +1=8 →8, carry 0..\n\n9. Hundred millions:1 +2=3 →3..\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the right, the sum is 3 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),7 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),6 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),4 (hundreds),0 (tens),0 (ones). Wait, wait, but the carryover from millions was 1 added to ten millions place, which was 1+6=7 plus 1 gives 8. Then hundred millions is 1+2=3..\n\nWait, but the original numbers have:.\n\nFirst number: 119,427,193.\n\nWhich breaks down as:.\n\n1 (hundred millions).\n1 (ten millions).\n9 (millions).\n4 (hundred thousands).\n2 (ten thousands).\n7 (thousands).\n1 (hundreds).\n9 (tens).\n3 (ones).\n\nSecond number: 268,540,207.\n\nWhich breaks down as:.\n\n2 (hundred millions).\n6 (ten millions).\n8 (millions).\n5 (hundred thousands).\n4 (ten thousands).\n0 (thousands).\n2 (hundreds).\n0 (tens).\n7 (ones).\n\nSo when adding each position:.\n\nHundred millions: 1 +2 =3..\n\nTen millions:1 +6 =7. Then add the carryover from millions place, which was 1 (since millions place was 9+8=17, carryover 1). So 7 +1=8..\n\nMillions:9 +8=17, write 7, carryover 1..\n\nHundred thousands:4 +5=9..\n\nTen thousands:2 +4=6..\n\nThousands:7 +0=7..\n\nHundreds:1 +2=3..\n\nTens:9 +0=9, then add the carryover from the previous (tens place was 9+0=9 +1 from ones carryover=10, so tens digit is 0, carryover 1. Wait, wait, I think I made a mistake earlier..\n\nWait, let's redo the addition step by step correctly, because maybe I messed up the positions..\n\nLet me write both numbers aligned:.\n\n          1 1 9 4 2 7 1 9 3.\n        + 2 6 8 5 4 0 2 0 7.\n        --------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):.\n\n3 +7 =10. Write 0, carryover 1..\n\nNext (tens):.\n\n9 +0 =9, plus carryover 1 =10. Write 0, carryover 1..\n\nNext (hundreds):.\n\n1 +2 =3, plus carryover 1 =4. Write 4, no carryover..\n\nNext (thousands):.\n\n7 +0 =7. Write 7..\n\nNext (ten thousands):.\n\n2 +4 =6. Write 6..\n\nNext (hundred thousands):.\n\n4 +5 =9. Write 9..\n\nNext (millions):.\n\n9 +8 =17. Write 7, carryover 1..\n\nNext (ten millions):.\n\n1 +6 =7, plus carryover 1 =8. Write 8..\n\nNext (hundred millions):.\n\n1 +2 =3. Write 3..\n\nSo combining all digits from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\n0 (ones), 0 (tens), 4 (hundreds),7 (thousands),6 (ten thousands),9 (hundred thousands),7 (millions),8 (ten millions),3 (hundred millions)..\n\nWait, but the millions digit was written as 7 with a carryover, then ten millions is 8, hundred millions is 3</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]  4%|3         | 18/500 [01:40<26:19,  3.28s/it]
