\n\nLet's list both numbers digit by digit from right to left (units to higher places):.\n\nFirst number: 977,289,657  .\nDigits (right to left): 7 (units),5 (tens),6 (hundreds),9 (thousands),8 (ten thousands),2 (hundred thousands),7 (millions),7 (ten millions),9 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number:122,353,274  .\nDigits (right to left):4 (units),7 (tens),2 (hundreds),3 (thousands),5 (ten thousands),3 (hundred thousands),2 (millions),2 (ten millions),1 (hundred millions).\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\n1. Units:7+4=11 →1, carry 1  .\n2. Tens:5+7=12 +1=13 →3, carry1  .\n3. Hundreds:6+2=8 +1=9 →9, carry0  .\n4. Thousands:9+3=12 →2, carry1  .\n5. Ten thousands:8+5=13 +1=14 →4, carry1  .\n6. Hundred thousands:2+3=5 +1=6 →6, carry0  .\n7. Millions:7+2=9 →9, carry0  .\n8. Ten millions:7+2=9 +0=9 →9, carry0  .\n9. Hundred millions:9+1=10 →0, carry1  .\n\nWait, but the hundred millions place: first number has 9, second has 1. 9+1=10, so we write 0 and carry 1. Then, since there are no higher digits, that carryover becomes a new digit at the beginning. So the result is 1 followed by the digits we have..\n\nPutting it all together from right to left (after adding):.\n\nUnits:1  .\nTens:3  .\nHundreds:9  .\nThousands:2  .\nTen thousands:4  .\nHundred thousands:6  .\nMillions:9  .\nTen millions:9  .\nHundred millions:0  .\nAnd the carryover 1 becomes a new digit: 1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
