ns (from right to left, ones to hundred millions):.\nOnes: 9.\nTens: 6.\nHundreds: 7.\nThousands: 4.\nTen-thousands: 7.\nHundred-thousands: 0.\nMillions: 9.\nTen-millions: 6.\nHundred-millions: 3.\n\nSecond number: 558,222,419.\n\nPositions:.\nOnes: 9.\nTens: 1.\nHundreds: 4.\nThousands: 2.\nTen-thousands: 2.\nHundred-thousands: 2.\nMillions: 8.\nTen-millions: 5.\nHundred-millions: 5.\n\nWait, but when adding, we can just go digit by digit from right to left, carrying over as needed. Let me try again step by step..\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\n1. Ones place: 9 (from first) + 9 (from second) = 18. Write 8, carry over 1..\n\n2. Tens place: 6 (from first) + 1 (from second) + carry 1 = 8. Write 8, no carry..\n\n3. Hundreds place: 7 (first) + 4 (second) = 11. Write 1, carry 1..\n\n4. Thousands place: 4 (first) + 2 (second) + carry 1 = 7. Write 7, no carry..\n\nWait, wait a second, I think I messed up here. Let me check again. Wait, the thousands place in the first number is 4? Let me confirm. First number is 369,074,769. Breaking it down:.\n\nFrom right (ones) to left:.\n\nPositions:.\n\n1: 9 (ones).\n2: 6 (tens).\n3: 7 (hundreds).\n4: 4 (thousands).\n5: 7 (ten thousands).\n6: 0 (hundred thousands).\n7: 9 (millions).\n8: 6 (ten millions).\n9: 3 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 558,222,419..\n\nPositions:.\n\n1:9 (ones).\n2:1 (tens).\n3:4 (hundreds).\n4:2 (thousands).\n5:2 (ten thousands).\n6:2 (hundred thousands).\n7:8 (millions).\n8:5 (ten millions).\n9:5 (hundred millions).\n\nSo when adding, the thousands place is position 4: 4 (from first) and 2 (from second). So 4 + 2 = 6, plus any carry-over from the previous step. Wait, previous step was hundreds place where we had 7 +4=11, so carry 1. So thousands place: 4 + 2 + 1 (carry) = 7. So write 7, no carry-over. Got it..\n\nThen the ten-thousands place: 7 (first) + 2 (second) = 9. No carry-over. So write 9..\n\nNext, hundred-thousands place: 0 (first) + 2 (second) = 2. Write 2..\n\nMillions place: 9 (first) +8 (second) = 17. Write 7, carry over 1..\n\nTen-millions place:6 (first) +5 (second) +1 (carry) = 12. Write 2, carry over 1..\n\nHundred-millions place:3 (first) +5 (second) +1 (carry) =9. Write 9..\n\nPutting all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nTens:8.\n\nHundreds:1 (with carry 1).\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen-thousands:9.\n\nHundred-thousands:2.\n\nMillions:7 (carry 1).\n\nTen-millions:2 (carry 1).\n\nHundred-millions:9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]  7%|6         | 33/500 [02:22<20:49,  2.68s/it]
