ve a carry-over. Wait, the previous step (tens) was 2 + 4 = 6 + 1 (carryover from ones) =7, so no new carry-over. So here, hundreds place: 1 + 9 = 10. So we write 0 in the hundreds place and carry over 1..\n\nNext is thousands place. Let's see the digits here. The first number: 146,694,123. Let's break it down:.\n\n146,694,123:.\n\n- Ones: 3.\n\n- Tens: 2.\n\n- Hundreds: 1.\n\n- Thousands: 4 (the next digit to the left is 4, from the thousands place: 694,123 → 4 is in thousands).\n\nWait, maybe it's easier to write both numbers aligned:.\n\nFirst number: 146,694,123.\n\nSecond number: 431,280,949.\n\nLet me write them out digit by digit, aligning the places:.\n\n          1 4 6 6 9 4 1 2 3.\n\n        +4 3 1 2 8 0 9 4 9.\n\nBut wait, let's check the digits properly. Let's count the digits:.\n\n146,694,123: 9 digits (1-4-6-6-9-4-1-2-3).\n\n431,280,949: 9 digits (4-3-1-2-8-0-9-4-9).\n\nYes, both are 9-digit numbers. So aligning:.\n\nDigit positions (from right, ones as position 1):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 3 and 9.\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 2 and 4.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 1 and 9.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands): 4 and 9.\n\nWait, no. Wait, let's list the digits properly. Let's take the first number 146,694,123..\n\nBreaking it down from right to left (ones to higher places):.\n\n- Position 1 (ones): 3.\n\n- Position 2 (tens): 2.\n\n- Position 3 (hundreds): 1.\n\n- Position 4 (thousands): 4.\n\n- Position 5 (ten thousands): 9.\n\n- Position 6 (hundred thousands): 6.\n\n- Position 7 (millions): 6.\n\n- Position 8 (ten millions): 4.\n\n- Position 9 (hundred millions): 1.\n\nSimilarly, the second number 431,280,949:.\n\n- Position 1: 9.\n\n- Position 2: 4.\n\n- Position 3: 9.\n\n- Position 4: 0.\n\n- Position 5: 8.\n\n- Position 6: 2.\n\n- Position 7: 1.\n\n- Position 8: 3.\n\n- Position 9: 4.\n\nWait, let me verify that. Let's write out the second number:.\n\n431,280,949..\n\nBreaking down:.\n\nFrom right to left (ones place first):.\n\nDigits are 9 (position 1), 4 (position 2), 9 (position 3), 0 (position 4), 8 (position 5), 2 (position 6), 1 (position 7), 3 (position 8), 4 (position 9)..\n\nSo for the thousands place (position 4), first number has 4, second number has 0..\n\nSo position 4: thousands place: 4 (from first) + 0 (from second) = 4. But wait, we had a carry-over of 1 from the hundreds place (position 3). So adding that carry-over: 4 + 0 +1 =5. So thousands place is 5, no carry-over..\n\nWait, let's step through each position again to make sure I don't get confused..\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 3 +9=12 → write 2, carry 1..\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 2 +4=6 +1=7 → write 7, carry 0..\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):1 +9=10 → write 0, carry 1..\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):4 (from first number) +0 (from second) +1 (carry) =5 → write 5, carry 0..\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):9 (from first) +8 (from second) → 9+8=17 → write 7, carry 1..\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):6 (from first) +2 (from second) +1 (carry) →6+2=8 +1=9 → write 9, carry 0..\n\nPosition 7 (millions):6 (from first) +1 (from second) →6+1=7 → write 7, carry 0..\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):4 (from first) +3 (from second) →4+3=7 → write 7, carry 0..\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):1 (from first) +4 (from second) →1+4=5 → write 5, carry 0..\n\nSo putting all the digits together from position 9 to 1:.\n\n5 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands),7 (ten thousands),5 (thousands),0 (hundreds),7 (tens),2 (ones)..\n\nWait, let me verify:.\n\nWait, after adding each position:.\n\nPosition 9: 1 +4=5..\n\nPosition8:4+3=7..\n\nPosition7:6+1=7..\n\nPosition6:6+2=8 plus carry 1? Wait, wait, earlier steps:.\n\nWait, position 5 was 9 (from first number) +8 (from second) →17. So wrote 7, carry 1..\n\nThen position6: first number's hundred thousands place is 6, second's is 2. So 6+2=8, plus carry 1=9. So 9, carry 0..\n\nPosition7: first's millions place is 6, second's is 1. 6+1=7. No carry..\n\nPosition8: first's ten millions is4, second's is3. 4+3=7..\n\nPosition9: first's hundred millions is1, second's is4. 1+4=5..\n\nThen the rest of the digits: thousands place (position4):5, ten thousands (position5):7, hundred thousands (position6):9, millions (position7):7, ten millions (position8):7, hundred millions (position9):5..\n\nThen the lower places:.\n\nthousands (position4):5.\n\nhundreds (position3):0.\n\ntens (position2):7.\n\nones (position1):2.\n\nWait, so putting all together:.\n\nFrom highest to lowest (left to right):.\n\nHundred millions (5), ten millions (7), millions (7), hundred thousands (9), ten thousands (7), thousands (5), hundreds (0), tens (7), ones (2)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]  9%|9         | 47/500 [03:00<19:22,  2.57s/it] 10%|9         | 48/500 [03:02<19:07,  2.54s/it]
