73,169.\n\nDigits from right to left:.\n\n9 (ones), 6 (tens), 1 (hundreds), 3 (thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 8 (hundred thousands), 2 (millions), 9 (ten millions), 7 (hundred millions).\n\nNow adding each digit with carry:.\n\nStart with ones place:.\n\n6 + 9 = 15 → 5, carry 1.\n\nTens: 8 + 6 = 14 + 1 (carry) = 15 → 5, carry 1.\n\nHundreds: 7 + 1 = 8 + 1 = 9 → 9, carry 0.\n\nThousands: 4 + 3 = 7 → 7, carry 0.\n\nTen thousands: 2 + 7 = 9 → 9, carry 0.\n\nHundred thousands: 4 + 8 = 12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nMillions: 9 + 2 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nTen millions: 4 + 9 = 13 +1 =14 →4, carry 1.\n\nHundred millions:6 +7=13 +1=14 →4, carry1.\n\nNow, since we're at the highest digit, the carryover 1 needs to be added as a new digit to the left. So the result starts with 1, then the hundred millions digit is 4, etc..\n\nPutting all together:.\n\n1 (from the last carry) 4 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),9 (hundreds),5 (tens),5 (ones). Wait, let me check the order again..\n\nWait, when we add digits, the first digit we get is ones place, then tens, etc. So when writing the final number, the digits are in reverse order of the steps. Let me list the digits as we computed them:.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nTens:5.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:9.\n\nHundred thousands:2 (with a carryover from here).\n\nMillions:2 (carryover here).\n\nTen millions:4 (carryover here).\n\nHundred millions:4 (carryover here).\n\nAnd then the final carryover 1 becomes the next digit, so billion place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
