n- 5 (ten thousands).\n- 1 (thousands).\n- 4 (hundreds).\n- 6 (tens).\n- 5 (ones).\n\nAnd 745,798,691:.\n\n- 7 (hundred millions).\n- 4 (ten millions).\n- 5 (millions).\n- 7 (hundred thousands).\n- 9 (ten thousands).\n- 8 (thousands).\n- 6 (hundreds).\n- 9 (tens).\n- 1 (ones).\n\nWait, maybe I should write them out with commas to see each digit's place properly:.\n\nFirst number: 440,751,465.\n\nDigits (from right to left):.\n\nOnes:5, Tens:6, Hundreds:4, Thousands:1, Ten thousands:5, Hundred thousands:7, Millions:0, Ten millions:4, Hundred millions:4..\n\nSecond number:745,798,691.\n\nDigits:.\n\nOnes:1, Tens:9, Hundreds:6, Thousands:8, Ten thousands:9, Hundred thousands:7, Millions:5, Ten millions:4, Hundred millions:7..\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\n5 +1 =6 (no carry).\n\nTens:6 +9=15. Write 5, carry 1..\n\nHundreds:4 +6=10 +1=11. Write 1, carry 1..\n\nThousands:1 +8=9 +1=10. Write 0, carry 1..\n\nTen thousands:5 +9=14 +1=15. Write5, carry1..\n\nHundred thousands:7 +7=14 +1=15. Write5, carry1..\n\nMillions place:0 +5=5 +1=6. No carry here..\n\nTen millions:4 +4=8. No carry..\n\nHundred millions:4 +7=11. Since these are the highest digits, we just write 11 here</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
