messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 745138857 and 996137931?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let's see. I need to add 745,138,857 and 996,137,931. Hmm, adding two large numbers like this. Let me start by writing them down properly aligned to make sure I add each digit correctly..\n\nFirst, I'll line them up by place value:.\n\n      7 4 5 1 3 8 8 5 7.\n    + 9 9 6 1 3 7 9 3 1.\n    -------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nOnes place: 7 + 1 = 8. So the ones digit is 8, no carry-over..\n\nTens place: 5 + 3 = 8. Tens digit is 8..\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 9 = 17. Wait, 8 + 9 is 17. So I write down 7 and carry over 1 to the thousands place..\n\nThousands place: 8 (from first number) + 7 (from second number) plus the carried 1. So 8 + 7 = 15, plus 1 is 16. So here, we write 6 and carry over 1..\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 + 3 = 6, plus the carry 1 makes 7. So 7 here, no carry..\n\nHundred-thousands place: 1 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) = 2. So 2 here..\n\nMillions place: 5 (from first) + 6 (from second). Wait, wait, let me check again. Wait, the numbers are 745,138,857 and 996,137,931. Let me break them down digit by digit to ensure I'm not mixing up places..\n\nWait, maybe I should list each digit position properly to avoid confusion. Let's write both numbers digit by digit:.\n\nFirst number: 7 4 5 1 3 8 8 5 7.\n\nSecond number:9 9 6 1 3 7 9 3 1.\n\nSo positions from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\nOnes: 7 +1 =8.\n\nTens:5 +3=8.\n\nHundreds:8 +9=17 (carry 1).\n\nThousands:8 +7 +1=16 (carry 1).\n\nTen-thousands:3 +3 +1=7.\n\nHundred-thousands:1 +7=8.\n\nMillions:5 +9=14 (carry 1).\n\nTen-millions:4 +9 +1=14 (carry 1).\n\nHundred-millions:7 +9 +1=17.\n\nWait, but hold on. Let me check each position again carefully:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n1. Ones place: 7 (from first number) + 1 (from second) = 8. Correct..\n\n2. Tens place: 5 (from first) +3 (from second) =8. Correct..\n\n3. Hundreds place:8 (first) +9 (second) =17. So digit is 7, carryover 1..\n\n4. Thousands place:8 (first) +7 (second) +1 (carry) =16. Digit 6, carry 1..\n\n5. Ten-thousands place:3 (first) +3 (second) +1 (carry) =7. Correct..\n\n6. Hundred-thousands place:1 (first) +7 (second) =8. Wait, but wait, the original numbers: first number is 745,138,857. Let's split into digits:.\n\nFirst number: 7 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 8 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 7 (ones)..\n\nSecond number:9 (hundred millions),9 (ten millions),6 (millions),1 (hundred thousands),3 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),9 (hundreds),3 (tens),1 (ones)..\n\nWait, so when adding each position:.\n\nWait, perhaps I got the places wrong earlier. Let me redo this properly, aligning each digit:.\n\nFirst number: 745,138,857.\n\nDigits (from left to right):.\n\n7 (hundred millions).\n\n4 (ten millions).\n\n5 (millions).\n\n1 (hundred thousands).\n\n3 (ten thousands).\n\n8 (thousands).\n\n8 (hundreds).\n\n5 (tens).\n\n7 (ones).\n\nSecond number:996,137,931.\n\nDigits:.\n\n9 (hundred millions).\n\n9 (ten millions).\n\n6 (millions).\n\n1 (hundred thousands).\n\n3 (ten thousands).\n\n7 (thousands).\n\n9 (hundreds).\n\n3 (tens).\n\n1 (ones).\n\nSo when adding, the corresponding digits are:.\n\nHundred millions:7 +9.\n\nTen millions:4 +9.\n\nMillions:5 +6.\n\nHundred thousands:1 +1.\n\nTen thousands:3 +3.\n\nThousands:8 +7.\n\nHundreds:8 +9.\n\nTens:5 +3.\n\nOnes:7 +1.\n\nWait, but earlier I was adding the digits from right to left (ones first). Let me do it that way again but correctly:.\n\nStarting from ones (rightmost):.\n\nOnes:7 +1=8..\n\nTens:5 +3=8..\n\nHundreds:8 +9=17 (7, carry 1)..\n\nThousands:8 +7=15 + carry 1=16 (6, carry 1)..\n\nTen-thousands:3 +3=6 +1=7..\n\nHundred-thousands:1 +1=2..\n\nMillions:5 +6=11 (1, carry 1)..\n\nTen millions:4 +9=13 +1=14 (4, carry 1)..\n\nHundred millions:7 +9=16 +1=17..\n\nWait, this seems different from before. Let me make sure:.\n\nWait, after hundreds place (carry 1), thousands place:8 (from first number) +7 (from second) +1 (carry) =16. So thousands digit is 6, carry 1..\n\nThen ten-thousands place:3 (first) +3 (second) +1 (carry) =7. Correct..\n\nHundred-thousands place:1 (first) +1 (second) =2. So here, no carry..\n\nMillions place:5 (first) +6 (second) =11. So write 1, carry 1..\n\nTen millions place:4 (first) +9 (second) =13 +1 (carry) =14. So write 4, carry 1..\n\nHundred millions place:7 (first) +9 (second) =16 +1 (carry) =17..\n\nSo putting all digits together from the highest place to lowest:.\n\nHundred millions:17.\n\nTen millions:14 (but the 1 is carried over, so actual digit here is 4 with carry 1).\n\nWait, no. Wait, when adding each digit, the carry propagates to the next higher place. Let me reconstruct the sum step by step:.\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\nOnes:7+1=8. Sum so far: 8..\n\nTens:5+3=8. Sum so far: 88..\n\nHundreds:8+9=17. Write 7, carry 1. Sum: 788..\n\nThousands:8+7=15 +1 (carry) =16. Write 6, carry 1. Sum: 6788..\n\nTen-thousands:3+3=6 +1=7. Sum:76788..\n\nHundred-thousands:1+1=2. Sum:276788..\n\nMillions:5+6=11. Write 1, carry 1. Sum: 1276788..\n\nTen millions:4+9=13 +1=14. Write 4, carry 1. Sum: 41276788..\n\nHundred millions:7+9=16 +1=17. Write 17</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 13%|#2        | 64/500 [03:53<25:52,  3.56s/it]
