7. Millions place: 0 + 8 = 8. Add carry 1 makes 9..\n8. Ten millions place: 6 + 9 = 15. Write 5, carry over 1..\n9. Hundred millions place: 3 + 8 = 11. Add carry 1 makes 12. Write 2, carry over 1. Wait, but there are no more digits left. So that carry-over 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
