(ten millions):2.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):6.\n\nSecond number:212,124,648.\n\nDigits:.\n\nPosition 1:8.\n\nPosition 2:4.\n\nPosition 3:6.\n\nPosition 4:4.\n\nPosition 5:2.\n\nPosition 6:1.\n\nPosition 7:2.\n\nPosition 8:1.\n\nPosition 9:2.\n\nSo aligning them:.\n\nPositions 9 to 1:.\n\nNumber1: 6 2 8 6 5 7 5 9 5.\n\nNumber2: 2 1 2 1 2 4 6 4 8.\n\nAdding each position starting from 1 (ones):.\n\n1. Position 1 (ones):5 +8=13 → 3, carry 1..\n\n2. Position 2 (tens):9 +4=13 +1=14 →4, carry1..\n\n3. Position3 (hundreds):5 +6=11 +1=12 →2, carry1..\n\n4. Position4 (thousands):7 +4=11 +1=12 →2, carry1..\n\n5. Position5 (ten thousands):5 +2=7 +1=8 →8, no carry..\n\nWait, wait, 5 (from first number) +2 (from second) +1 (carry) =8. So 8 here, carry 0..\n\n6. Position6 (hundred thousands):6 +4. Wait, no, the first number's hundred thousands digit is 7? Wait no, let me check again..\n\nWait, the first number is 628,657,595. Breaking it down:.\n\nHundred millions:6.\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:5.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nHundreds:5.\n\nTens:9.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nWait, no. Wait, the number is 628,657,595. So:.\n\nBreaking into groups:.\n\n628 (millions), 657 (thousands), 595 (units)..\n\nSo 628,657,595 is:.\n\n6 hundred millions.\n\n2 ten millions.\n\n8 millions.\n\n6 hundred thousands.\n\n5 ten thousands.\n\n7 thousands.\n\n5 hundreds.\n\n9 tens.\n\n5 ones..\n\nSimilarly, 212,124,648 is:.\n\n2 hundred millions.\n\n1 ten million.\n\n2 millions.\n\n1 hundred thousand.\n\n2 ten thousands.\n\n4 thousands.\n\n6 hundreds.\n\n4 tens.\n\n8 ones..\n\nSo aligning each digit position:.\n\nHundred millions:6 vs 2.\n\nTen millions:2 vs1.\n\nMillions:8 vs2.\n\nHundred thousands:6 vs1.\n\nTen thousands:5 vs2.\n\nThousands:7 vs4.\n\nHundreds:5 vs6.\n\nTens:9 vs4.\n\nOnes:5 vs8.\n\nSo adding each digit:.\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\n1. Ones:5+8=13 →3, carry1..\n\n2. Tens:9+4=13 +1=14 →4, carry1..\n\n3. Hundreds:5+6=11 +1=12 →2, carry1..\n\n4. Thousands:7+4=11 +1=12 →2, carry1..\n\n5. Ten thousands:5+2=7 +1=8 →8, carry0..\n\n6. Hundred thousands:6+1=7 +0=7 →7, carry0..\n\n7. Millions:8+2=10 →0, carry1..\n\n8. Ten millions:2+1=3 +1=4 →4, carry0..\n\n9. Hundred millions:6+2=8 +0=8 →8, no carry..\n\nPutting it all together from the highest digit:.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:0 (from 8+2=10, carry1).\n\nBut wait, millions digit was 8 (from first number) and 2 (from second), so 8+2=10, so write 0 and carry 1 to ten millions. Wait, no: the hundred millions digit is 6+2=8. Then ten millions is 2+1=3, plus the carry from millions place. Wait, maybe I messed up the order..\n\nWait, when adding, the carry propagates to the next higher digit. Let me redo the steps carefully:.\n\nPositions from ones (right) to left:.\n\n1. Ones:5+8=13 →3, carry1..\n\n2. Tens:9+4=13 +1=14 →4, carry1..\n\n3. Hundreds:5+6=11 +1=12 →2, carry1..\n\n4. Thousands:7+4=11 +1=12 →2, carry1..\n\n5. Ten thousands:5+2=7 +1=8 →8, carry0..\n\n6. Hundred thousands:6+1=7 +0=7 →7, carry0..\n\n7. Millions:8+2=10 →0, carry1..\n\n8. Ten millions:2+1=3 +1 (carry from millions) =4 →4, carry0..\n\n9. Hundred millions:6+2=8 +0=8 →8..\n\nSo the result digits from left to right (hundred millions to ones):.\n\n8 (hundred millions).\n\n4 (ten millions).\n\n0 (millions).\n\n7 (hundred thousands).\n\n8 (ten thousands).\n\n2 (thousands).\n\n2 (hundreds).\n\n4 (tens).\n\n3 (ones).\n\nWait, but let's check that:.\n\nWait, after adding the millions place:8 (from first number) +2 (from second) =10. So write 0 in millions place, carry 1 to ten millions..\n\nTen millions place: original digits 2 (first) +1 (second) =3, plus carry 1 =4. So ten millions digit is 4..\n\nHundred millions:6+2=8..\n\nSo combining:.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:0.\n\nHundred thousands:6 (from first) +1 (second) =7.\n\nTen thousands:5 (first) +2 (second)=7, but earlier step said 5+2=7, plus carry from thousands? Wait, earlier steps had ten thousands as 5+2=7 plus carry 1? Wait, no..\n\nWait, let me retrace:.\n\nAfter thousands place:7+4=11 +1 (carry from hundreds) →12, so carry1 to ten thousands..\n\nTen thousands place:5 +2=7 +1 (carry from thousands)=8. So that's correct. So ten thousands digit is 8, no carry..\n\nThen hundred thousands:6 (first) +1 (second) =7, plus carry 0 →7..\n\nMillions:8+2=10 →0, carry1..\n\nTen millions:2+1=3 +1=4..\n\nHundred millions:6+2=8..\n\nSo the digits are:.\n\n8 (hundred millions).\n\n4 (ten millions).\n\n0 (millions).\n\n7 (hundred thousands).\n\n8 (ten thousands).\n\n2 (thousands).\n\n2 (hundreds).\n\n4 (tens).\n\n3 (ones).\n\nWait, but the thousands digit was calculated as 2 (from thousands place:7+4=11 +1=12 →2, carry1). Then ten thousands place:5+2=7 +1=8. So thousands digit is 2, ten thousands is 8</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 15%|#4        | 74/500 [04:19<18:30,  2.61s/it] 15%|#5        | 75/500 [04:22<18:06,  2.56s/it]
