.\nTen thousands:5.\nThousands:1.\nHundreds:5.\nTens:9.\nOnes:8.\n\nSimilarly, 176,145,867:.\n\nHundred millions:1.\nTen millions:7.\nMillions:6.\nHundred thousands:1.\nTen thousands:4.\nThousands:5.\nHundreds:8.\nTens:6.\nOnes:7.\n\nSo when adding, each corresponding place:.\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\nOnes: 8 +7 =15 (write 5, carry 1).\nTens:9 +6 +1=16 (write 6, carry 1).\nHundreds:5 +8 +1=14 (write 4, carry 1).\nThousands:1 +5 +1=7 (no carry).\nWait, thousands place? Wait, the thousands place in first number is 1 (from 691,851,598 which is ... let me check again. Wait 691,851,598: the digits are 6 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 8 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 8 (ones). So yes, thousands place is 1. The second number 176,145,867: thousands place is 5. So 1 +5=6, plus any carryover from the hundreds place. Wait, the hundreds place sum was 14, which carried over 1. So thousands place would be 1 (from first number) +5 (from second) +1 (carry) =7. So thousands place is 7, carry 0..\n\nThen ten thousands place: first number has 5, second has 4. So 5+4=9, plus carryover 0. So 9..\n\nHundred thousands place: first number has 8, second has 1. 8+1=9..\n\nMillions place: first number has 1, second has 6. 1+6=7..\n\nTen millions place: first number has 9, second has 7. 9+7=16. So write 6, carryover 1..\n\nHundred millions place: first number has 6, second has 1. 6+1=7 plus the carryover 1 makes 8..\n\nPutting it all together from the highest place to the lowest:.\n\nHundred millions:8.\nTen millions:6.\nMillions:7.\nHundred thousands:9.\nTen thousands:9.\nThousands:7.\nHundreds:4.\nTens:6.\nOnes:5.\n\nWait, but let me check again. Let me write each step properly with carryover:.\n\nStart from ones:.\n\n1. Ones: 8 +7 =15 → 5, carry 1.\n2. Tens:9 +6 +1 =16 →6, carry1.\n3. Hundreds:5 +8 +1 =14 →4, carry1.\n4. Thousands:1 +5 +1=7 →7, carry0.\n5. Ten thousands:5 +4=9 →9, carry0.\n6. Hundred thousands:8 +1=9 →9, carry0.\n7. Millions:1 +6=7 →7, carry0.\n8. Ten millions:9 +7=16 →6, carry1.\n9. Hundred millions:6 +1 +1=8 →8, carry0.\n\nSo combining all the digits starting from hundred millions down: 8 (hundred millions), 6 (ten millions),7 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),9 (ten thousands),7 (thousands),4 (hundreds),6 (tens),5 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 17%|#7        | 85/500 [04:48<18:15,  2.64s/it]
