s:.\n\n721,785,238:.\n\nHundred millions: 7.\nTen millions: 2.\nMillions: 1.\nHundred thousands: 7.\nTen thousands: 8.\nThousands: 5.\nHundreds: 2.\nTens: 3.\nOnes: 8.\n\n122,585,810:.\n\nHundred millions: 1.\nTen millions: 2.\nMillions: 2.\nHundred thousands: 5.\nTen thousands: 8.\nThousands: 5.\nHundreds: 8.\nTens: 1.\nOnes: 0.\n\nWait, maybe that's a better way. Let's align each position:.\n\nHundred millions: 7 + 1 = ?.\nTen millions: 2 + 2 = ?.\nMillions: 1 + 2 = ?.\nHundred thousands:7 +5= ?.\nTen thousands:8 +8= ?.\nThousands:5 +5= ?.\nHundreds:2 +8= ?.\nTens:3 +1= ?.\nOnes:8 +0=8..\n\nWait, but when adding, we have to consider any carry-over from the previous addition. Let me go step by step starting from the ones..\n\nOnes place: 8 + 0 = 8. No carry-over..\n\nTens place: 3 + 1 = 4. No carry-over..\n\nHundreds place: 2 + 8 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1..\n\nThousands place: 5 +5 =10, plus the carry-over 1 makes 11. Write 1, carry over 1..\n\nTen thousands place:8 +8=16, plus carry-over 1 is 17. Write 7, carry over 1..\n\nHundred thousands place:7 +5=12, plus carry-over 1 is 13. Write 3, carry over 1..\n\nMillions place:1 (from first number) +2 (from second number)=3, plus carry-over 1 makes 4. Wait, hold on. Let me check the positions again..\n\nWait, the first number is 721,785,238. Let's break it down as:.\n\nHundred millions:7.\nTen millions:2.\nMillions:1.\nHundred thousands:7.\nTen thousands:8.\nThousands:5.\nHundreds:2.\nTens:3.\nOnes:8.\n\nThe second number is 122,585,810:.\n\nHundred millions:1.\nTen millions:2.\nMillions:2.\nHundred thousands:5.\nTen thousands:8.\nThousands:5.\nHundreds:8.\nTens:1.\nOnes:0.\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nStarting from ones as before, up through the digits..\n\nAfter the hundreds thousands place, which was 7 (from first number) +5 (from second) plus carry 1 gives 13. So write 3, carry 1..\n\nNow moving to the millions place. The first number has 1 in the millions place, and the second has 2. So 1 +2 =3, plus the carried 1 makes 4. So write 4, no carry-over? Wait, 1+2=3, plus 1 is 4. So that's correct. So millions place is 4..\n\nThen ten millions place: first number has 2, second has 2. 2+2=4. No carry-over. So ten millions place is 4..\n\nHundred millions place:7 +1=8. So that's 8..\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum is:.\n\nHundred millions:8.\nTen millions:4.\nMillions:4.\nHundred thousands:3.\nTen thousands:7.\nThousands:1.\nHundreds:0.\nTens:4.\nOnes:8.\n\nWait, let me check the digits again. Let's reconstruct the sum:.\n\nFrom right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\nOnes:8.\nTens:4.\nHundreds:0.\nThousands:1.\nTen thousands:7.\nHundred thousands:3.\nMillions:4.\nTen millions:4.\nHundred millions:8</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 19%|#8        | 94/500 [05:22<21:56,  3.24s/it]
