messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 872662112 and 913627987?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let's see. I need to add 872,662,112 and 913,627,987. Hmm, adding two large numbers. Alright, let me start by writing them down one under the other to line up the digits properly..\n\nSo:.\n\n  872,662,112.\n+ 913,627,987.\n----------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. Let's add each column step by step, remembering to carry over if the sum is 10 or more..\n\nFirst, the ones place: 2 + 7. That equals 9. So the ones digit of the sum is 9. No carry-over here..\n\nNext, the tens place: 1 (from the first number) plus 8 (from the second number). 1 + 8 is 9. So the tens digit is 9 again. Still no carry-over..\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 1 + 9. That's 10. Oh, wait, here we have a sum of 10. So we write down 0 in the hundreds place and carry over 1 to the thousands place..\n\nThousands place: Now, the first number has a 2 there, and the second has 7. Adding them gives 2 + 7 = 9, plus the carried-over 1 makes 10. Again, write 0 here and carry over 1 to the next place (ten-thousands)..\n\nTen-thousands place: The first number has 6 here, the second has 8. 6 + 8 = 14, plus the carry-over 1 is 15. So write 5 here and carry over 1..\n\nHundred-thousands place: The first number has 6, the second 2. 6 + 2 = 8, plus the carry 1 makes 9. So that's 9 here, no carry-over..\n\nMillions place: First number is 2, second is 6. 2 + 6 = 8. Wait, but wait, let me check the positions again. Wait, the numbers are:.\n\nFirst number: 872,662,112.\n\nBreaking it down: 8 (hundred millions), 7 (ten millions), 2 (millions), then 6 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 2 (ones)..\n\nSecond number: 913,627,987.\n\nBreaking down: 9 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 7 (ones)..\n\nSo when adding the millions place: first number is 2 (from 872 million), second is 3 (from 913 million). 2 + 3 = 5. But wait, earlier I thought there was a carry-over here. Wait, let's retrace..\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the previous steps. Let me go through each digit carefully again, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 2 +7 =9 (correct)..\n\nTens place:1 +8=9 (correct)..\n\nHundreds place:1 +9=10. So 0 here, carry 1..\n\nThousands place:2 (from first number's thousands place) +7 (second number's thousands place) =9. Then plus the carried 1: total 10. So 0 here, carry 1. Wait, earlier I thought first number's thousands digit was 2. Let me check:.\n\nFirst number: 872,662,112. Breaking down:.\n\nDigits from right (ones place):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):2.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):1.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):1.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):2.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):6.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):6.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):2.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):7.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):8.\n\nSecond number:913,627,987..\n\nDigits from right:.\n\nPosition 1:7.\n\nPosition 2:8.\n\nPosition3:9.\n\nPosition4:7.\n\nPosition5:2.\n\nPosition6:6.\n\nPosition7:3.\n\nPosition8:1.\n\nPosition9:9.\n\nSo when adding each position:.\n\n1. Ones:2+7=9.\n\n2. Tens:1+8=9.\n\n3. Hundreds:1+9=10 → 0, carry 1.\n\n4. Thousands:2 (from first) +7 (from second) =9 +1=10 → 0, carry1.\n\n5. Ten thousands:6 (first) +2 (second) =8 +1 (carry) =9. No carry..\n\n6. Hundred thousands:6 (first) +6 (second) =12. So 2, carry1..\n\n7. Millions:2 (first) +3 (second) =5 +1=6. No carry..\n\n8. Ten millions:7 (first) +1 (second) =8. No carry..\n\n9. Hundred millions:8 (first) +9 (second) =17. So 7, carry1..\n\nWait, but after the hundred millions place, there's no higher digits, so the carry 1 becomes a new digit at the billions place..\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\nPositions (right to left):.\n\n1:9.\n\n2:9.\n\n3:0 (carry1).\n\n4:0 (carry1).\n\n5:9.\n\n6:2 (carry1 from previous step).\n\n7:6 (no carry).\n\n8:8.\n\n9:7 (from 8+9=17, so 7 here and carry1).\n\nThen the carry1 becomes the billions place:1..\n\nSo the total sum would be 1,7 (billion), then 8 (hundred million), 8 (ten million), 6 (million), 2 (hundred thousand), 9 (ten thousand), 0 (thousand), 0 (hundred),9 (ten),9 (one)..\n\nWait, let me arrange the digits properly after each step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:9.\n\nTens:9.\n\nHundreds:0 (carry1 to thousands).\n\nThousands:2 (from first) +7 (second) =9 +1 (carry) =10 → 0, carry1 to ten thousands..\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the positions. Let me write all digits step by step:.\n\nFirst number: 872,662,112 → digits in order (from hundred millions to ones):.\n\n8,7,2,6,6,2,1,1,2.\n\nSecond number:913,627,987 → digits:.\n\n9,1,3,6,2,7,9,8,7.\n\nAdding each corresponding digit, starting from the right (ones place):.\n\nPosition 9 (ones):.\n\n2 +7 =9.\n\nPosition8 (tens):.\n\n1 +8=9.\n\nPosition7 (hundreds):.\n\n1 +9=10 → 0, carry1.\n\nPosition6 (thousands):.\n\n2 +7=9 +1 (carry) =10 →0, carry1.\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\n\n6 +2=8 +1=9, carry0.\n\nPosition4 (hundred thousands):.\n\n6 +6=12 →2, carry1.\n\nPosition3 (millions):.\n\n2 +3=5 +1=6, carry0.\n\nPosition2 (ten millions):.\n\n7 +1=8, carry0.\n\nPosition1 (hundred millions):.\n\n8 +9=17 →7, carry1.\n\nNow, since we have a carry1 at the hundred millions place (position1), we add a new digit at the billions place:1..\n\nSo combining all digits from left to right:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:7.\n\nTen millions:8.\n\nMillions:6.\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nTen thousands:9.\n\nThousands:0.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nTens:9.\n\nOnes:9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 19%|#9        | 95/500 [05:25<20:31,  3.04s/it]
