st number has 1, and the second has 9. 1 + 9 = 10. So we write 0 here and carry over 1, but since there are no higher places left, we add that 1 at the beginning. Wait, but how does that work? Let me check again..\n\nWait, actually, when adding the hundred-millions place: 1 (from 130,037,904) and 9 (from 963,899,905) gives 10. So we put 0 there and carry over 1 to the next higher place, which would be the billions place. Since there are no other digits, we just write that carried 1 in front. So the final sum should start with 1 followed by 0 in the hundred-millions place</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
