ndreds: 0.\n\nThousands: 4.\n\nTen thousands: 1.\n\nHundred thousands: 4.\n\nMillions: 6.\n\nTen millions: 5.\n\nHundred millions: 7.\n\nWait, but the order when writing the number is from highest place to lowest. So the digits are:.\n\nHundred millions:7.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nMillions:6.\n\nHundred thousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nTens:4.\n\nOnes:5</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 21%|##1       | 105/500 [05:52<18:00,  2.74s/it] 21%|##1       | 106/500 [05:54<17:31,  2.67s/it]
