messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 607069464 and 799642630?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let me try to add these two numbers: 607,069,464 and 799,642,630. Hmm, adding large numbers can be tricky, but I'll take it step by step..\n\nFirst, I should write them down aligning the digits properly. Let's line them up by place value:.\n\n  607,069,464.\n+ 799,642,630.\n----------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. Let's check each digit one by one..\n\nOnes place: 4 (from the first number) + 0 (from the second) = 4. So the ones digit is 4. No carry-over here..\n\nTens place: 6 + 3 = 9. Tens digit is 9. Still no carry-over..\n\nHundreds place: 4 + 6 = 10. Oh, here we have a sum of 10. So we write down 0 and carry over 1 to the next place..\n\nThousands place: 6 (from first number) + 2 (from second) plus the carried 1 equals 9. So thousands digit is 9. Carry-over is 0 now..\n\nTen-thousands place: 9 + 6 = 15. Write down 5, carry over 1..\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 4 = 4, plus the carried 1 makes 5. So that's 5 here. No carry-over..\n\nMillions place: 7 + 9 = 16. Wait, wait. Wait, let me check the digits again. The first number is 607,069,464. Let me break it down:.\n\nDigits (from right to left):.\nPosition 1 (ones): 4.\nPosition 2 (tens): 6.\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 4.\nPosition 4 (thousands): 6.\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 9.\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 0.\nPosition 7 (millions): 7.\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 0.\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 6.\n\nWait, wait, maybe I got the places wrong. Let me make sure. Let's count each digit:.\n\nFirst number: 6 0 7 0 6 9 4 6 4. Wait, no, wait. Wait, 607,069,464. Let's separate the digits with commas as per standard:.\n\n607,069,464 is 607 million 69 thousand 464..\n\nSo breaking down:.\n\nHundred millions: 6.\nTen millions: 0.\nMillions: 7.\nHundred thousands: 0.\nTen thousands:6 .\nThousands:9.\nHundreds:4.\nTens:6.\nOnes:4.\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Wait, maybe I should write each digit position by position. Let's list each digit:.\n\nNumber 1: 6 0 7 0 6 9 4 6 4.\n\nPositions (from left to right):.\n\n1. 6 (hundred millions).\n2. 0 (ten millions).\n3. 7 (millions).\n4. 0 (hundred thousands).\n5. 6 (ten thousands).\n6. 9 (thousands).\n7. 4 (hundreds).\n8. 6 (tens).\n9. 4 (ones).\n\nNumber 2:7 9 9 6 4 2 6 3 0.\n\nBreaking down:.\n\n1. 7 (hundred millions).\n2. 9 (ten millions).\n3. 9 (millions).\n4. 6 (hundred thousands).\n5. 4 (ten thousands).\n6. 2 (thousands).\n7. 6 (hundreds).\n8. 3 (tens).\n9. 0 (ones).\n\nNow, adding each corresponding position starting from the right (ones place):.\n\nPosition 9 (ones): 4 + 0 = 4. Write down 4. Carry 0..\n\nPosition 8 (tens):6 +3=9. Write 9. Carry 0..\n\nPosition7 (hundreds):4+6=10. Write 0, carry 1..\n\nPosition6 (thousands):9 +2=11. Plus carry 1 makes 12. Write 2, carry 1..\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):6 +4=10. Plus carry 1=11. Write 1, carry 1..\n\nPosition4 (hundred thousands):0 +6=6. Plus carry 1=7. Write 7. Carry 0..\n\nPosition3 (millions):7 +9=16. Write 6, carry 1..\n\nPosition2 (ten millions):0 +9=9. Plus carry 1=10. Write 0, carry 1..\n\nPosition1 (hundred millions):6 +7=13. Plus carry 1=14. Write 4, carry 1. But since there are no higher places, we need to add that carry. So the final carry 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning..\n\nSo putting all the digits together with the carries:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:4.\n\nTens:9.\n\nHundreds:0.\n\nThousands:2 (from position6, which is thousands place).\n\nWait, wait, maybe I messed up the positions. Let me recheck:.\n\nWait, when we add, each position is:.\n\nPosition9 (ones):4+0=4.\n\nPosition8 (tens):6+3=9.\n\nPosition7 (hundreds):4+6=10 (carry 1).\n\nPosition6 (thousands):9+2=11 +1=12 (carry 1).\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):6+4=10 +1=11 (carry1).\n\nPosition4 (hundred thousands):0+6=6 +1=7 (no carry).\n\nPosition3 (millions):7+9=16 (carry1).\n\nPosition2 (ten millions):0+9=9 +1=10 (carry1).\n\nPosition1 (hundred millions):6+7=13 +1=14 (carry1). But after that, we have to add the carry. Wait, but hundred millions is the highest place here. So after adding the hundred millions digits (6+7=13 plus carry 1 makes 14), we write down 4, carry 1. Since there's no higher place, the carry 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning (billions place). So the total sum would be 1,4 followed by the rest..\n\nPutting all together:.\n\nFrom the billions place:1.\n\nThen hundred millions:4.\n\nTen millions:0 (from position2 sum:10, write 0 carry1, but that carry was added to hundred millions).\n\nWait, maybe I need to track each step again carefully..\n\nLet me write each step with the digits:.\n\nStart adding from right to left:.\n\nDigit 1 (ones): 4 +0=4. Sum digit:4. Carry:0..\n\nDigit2 (tens):6+3=9. Sum:9. Carry:0..\n\nDigit3 (hundreds):4+6=10. Sum:0. Carry:1..\n\nDigit4 (thousands):9 (from first number's thousands place) +2 (from second number's thousands place) =11. Add carry 1: total 12. Sum digit:2. Carry:1..\n\nDigit5 (ten thousands):6 (from first) +4 (from second) =10. Add carry 1:11. Sum:1. Carry:1..\n\nDigit6 (hundred thousands):0 (from first) +6 (from second)=6. Add carry1:7. Sum:7. Carry:0..\n\nDigit7 (millions):7 (from first) +9 (from second)=16. Sum:6. Carry:1..\n\nDigit8 (ten millions):0 (from first) +9 (from second)=9. Add carry1:10. Sum:0. Carry:1..\n\nDigit9 (hundred millions):6 (from first) +7 (from second)=13. Add carry1:14. Sum:4. Carry:1..\n\nNow, after the hundred millions place, there's a carry of1 left. Since there are no more digits, we add this as a new digit at the beginning (billions place)..\n\nSo the sum digits are:.\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 6 (millions),7 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),2 (thousands),0 (hundreds),9 (tens),4 (ones)..\n\nWait, wait, let me arrange them properly. Let's list the digits from highest place to lowest:.\n\n- Billions place:1.\n\n- Hundred millions:4.\n\n- Ten millions:0.\n\n- Millions:6.\n\n- Hundred thousands:7.\n\n- Ten thousands:1.\n\n- Thousands:2.\n\n- Hundreds:0.\n\n- Tens:9.\n\n- Ones:4.\n\nSo combining these: 1,407,712,094..\n\nWait, let me check that. Let's write the digits:.\n\nStarting from billions:.\n\n1 followed by 4 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 9 (tens), 4 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 25%|##4       | 123/500 [06:40<17:12,  2.74s/it]
