e first number is 2 (since it's 842,710,888: 8 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 2 (millions), ...). The second number's millions place is 1 (since it's 481,117,620: 4 (hundred millions),8 (ten millions),1 (millions), ...). So 2+1=3. So write 3, no carry..\n\nTen millions place:4 (first) +8 (second)=12. Write 2 here, carry 1..\n\nHundred millions place:8 (first) +4 (second)=12. Add the carry 1 makes 13. Write 3 here, carry 1. But there's no higher place, so we need to add that carry. So the final number would start with 1 followed by 3, then the rest..\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the hundred millions place:.\n\nWe have a carryover of 1, then 3 (from 8+4+1), then the ten millions digit is 2 (from 4+8=12, with 2 written and carry 1). Then millions digit 3, hundred thousands 8, ten thousands 2, thousands 8, hundreds 5, tens 0, ones 8. Wait, wait, let me recheck each step:.\n\nWait, when adding the hundred millions place: 8 (first) +4 (second)=12, plus the carryover 1 from the ten millions place? Wait, no. Wait, the order of addition is right to left, so when we get to the hundred millions place, we shouldn't have a carryover from the ten millions yet. Wait, perhaps I got the order mixed up..\n\nWait, maybe I should do this more carefully step by step, starting from the ones and moving left, keeping track of carryover each time..\n\nLet me write each digit position with their values:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):.\nFirst number:8.\nSecond:0.\nSum:8 +0 =8. Write 8. Carryover 0..\n\nPosition2 (tens):.\nFirst:8.\nSecond:2.\nSum:8+2=10. Write 0. Carryover 1..\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):.\nFirst:8.\nSecond:6.\nSum:8+6=14. Plus carry 1 is 15. Write 5. Carryover1..\n\nPosition4 (thousands):.\nFirst:0.\nSecond:7.\nSum:0+7=7. Plus carry 1=8. Write8. Carryover0..\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):.\nFirst:1.\nSecond:1.\nSum:1+1=2. Write2. Carryover0..\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):.\nFirst:7.\nSecond:1.\nSum:7+1=8. Write8. Carryover0..\n\nPosition7 (millions):.\nFirst:2.\nSecond:1.\nSum:2+1=3. Write3. Carryover0..\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):.\nFirst:4.\nSecond:8.\nSum:4+8=12. Write2. Carryover1..\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):.\nFirst:8.\nSecond:4.\nSum:8+4=12. Plus carryover1=13. Write3. Carryover1..\n\nNow, since we're at the leftmost digit, the carryover1 needs to be added as a new digit at the beginning. So the final sum is 1 (from carryover) followed by 3 (hundred millions), then the rest..\n\nPutting all the digits together from left to right:.\n\n1 (carry) 3 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions),3 (millions),8 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),5 (hundreds),0 (tens),8 (ones)..\n\nWait, but let me list each position's result:.\n\nHundred millions:13 (so 3 with carry 1).\nBut actually, after adding hundred millions place, we have 8+4=12 plus carry 1 from ten millions place, which was added in the ten millions step. Wait, no. Wait, the ten millions place addition gave a carryover of 1, which affects the hundred millions place..\n\nWait, no. Let me recheck the steps in order:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones: 8+0=8. Sum:8. Carry:0..\n\n2. Tens:8+2=10. Sum:0. Carry:1..\n\n3. Hundreds:8+6=14 +1=15. Sum:5. Carry:1..\n\n4. Thousands:0+7=7 +1=8. Sum:8. Carry:0..\n\n5. Ten thousands:1+1=2. Sum:2. Carry:0..\n\n6. Hundred thousands:7+1=8. Sum:8. Carry:0..\n\n7. Millions:2+1=3. Sum:3. Carry:0..\n\n8. Ten millions:4+8=12. Sum:2. Carry:1..\n\n9. Hundred millions:8+4=12. Now, here, the carry from ten millions is 1, so 12+1=13. Sum:3. Carry:1..\n\nNow, since we're done with all digits, the carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the front..\n\nSo the total sum is 1 followed by 3 (from hundred millions), then the rest as computed..\n\nSo putting all together: 1 3 2 (ten millions sum was 2?), wait, wait:.\n\nWait, after adding each position:.\n\nPositions (from right to left):.\n\n1. Ones:8.\n\n2. Tens:0.\n\n3. Hundreds:5.\n\n4. Thousands:8.\n\n5. Ten thousands:2.\n\n6. Hundred thousands:8.\n\n7. Millions:3.\n\n8. Ten millions:2 (from 4+8=12, so written digit is 2, carry 1).\n\n9. Hundred millions:8+4=12 plus carry 1=13, written digit 3, carry 1..\n\nThen, the final carry is 1, so the digits are:.\n\n1 (carry), 3 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions),3 (millions),8 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),5 (hundreds),0 (tens),8 (ones)..\n\nSo the sum is 1,328,828,508?.\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let's write each digit from left to right:.\n\nThe carryover 1 is the first digit, then the hundred millions place sum is 3, ten millions is 2, millions is 3, hundred thousands is8, ten thousands is2, thousands is8, hundreds is5, tens is0, ones is8</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 27%|##7       | 136/500 [07:16<18:17,  3.02s/it] 27%|##7       | 137/500 [07:19<17:46,  2.94s/it]
