ed thousand), 2 (ten thousand), 5 (thousand), 9 (hundred), 3 (ten), 0 (one)..\n\nWait, maybe I should list each digit position by position:.\n\nFirst number: 1 9 0 9 2 4 7 1 1.\n\nSecond number:2 4 2 8 2 5 9 3 0.\n\nPositions from left to right: hundred millions, ten millions, millions, hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands, hundreds, tens, ones..\n\nSo adding each corresponding digit:.\n\nStarting from the ones (rightmost):.\n\nOnes: 1 + 0 = 1.\n\nTens:1 +3 =4.\n\nHundreds:7 +9 =16 → 6, carry 1.\n\nThousands:4 +5 +1 (carry) =10 → 0, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands:2 +2 +1 =5 → wait, no. Wait, the thousands place was 4 (from first number) and 5 (from second), so after adding and carry, we had 10. Then the next digit is ten thousands place: first number's ten thousands digit is 2, second's is 2. So 2 +2 =4, plus the carry-over 1? Wait no, maybe I messed up the positions..\n\nWait, maybe I should break down each digit step by step properly..\n\nLet me write both numbers vertically:.\n\n  190,924,711.\n+242,825,930.\n-------------.\n\nAligning each digit:.\n\nPosition (from right, starting at 1):.\n\n1: 1 (ones) and 0 → sum 1.\n2: 1 (tens) and 3 → 4.\n3:7 (hundreds) and9 →16 →6, carry 1.\n4:4 (thousands) and5 →9 +1=10 →0, carry1.\n5:2 (ten thousands) and2 →4 +1=5.\n6:9 (hundred thousands) and8 →17 →7, carry1.\n7:0 (millions) and2 →2 +1=3.\n8:9 (ten millions) and4 →13 →3, carry1.\n9:1 (hundred millions) and2 →3 +1=4.\n\nWait, but when adding the millions place: first number's millions digit is 0, second's is 2. So 0 +2 =2, plus the carry-over 1 from the hundred thousands place (which was 9+8=17, carried 1). So that's 2 +1=3..\n\nThen ten millions place: first number's ten millions is 9, second's is 4. 9+4=13, write 3, carry 1..\n\nHundred millions place: 1 +2=3, plus the carry 1 →4..\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:1.\n\nTens:4.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nThousands:0.\n\nTen thousands:5.\n\nHundred thousands:7.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nTen millions: