lion, so the millions digit is 1). Adding those: 0 + 1 = 1. Plus the carryover 1 makes 2. So millions place is 2..\n\nTen millions place: First number has 9, second has 9 (since 691 million's ten millions place is 9). 9 + 9 = 18. Plus any carryover? No carryover here because the previous step was millions place which didn't carry. Wait, wait, earlier steps: When we did the hundred-thousands place, we had a carryover of 1. Wait, let me recount the steps properly. Maybe I made a mistake here..\n\nWait, let me redo this step by step to avoid confusion..\n\nLet me write both numbers vertically:.\n\n  290,279,142.\n+691,370,036.\n-------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\nOnes place: 2 + 6 = 8. No carryover..\n\nTens place: 4 + 3 = 7. No carryover..\n\nHundreds place: 1 + 0 = 1. No carryover..\n\nThousands place: 9 + 6 = 15. Write down 5, carry over 1..\n\nTen-thousands place: 7 + 3 = 10, plus the carryover 1 is 11. Write down 1, carry over 1..\n\nHundred-thousands place: 2 + 7 = 9, plus carryover 1 is 10. Write down 0, carry over 1..\n\nMillions place: 0 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) = 1, plus carryover 1 is 2. Write down 2, no carryover..\n\nTen millions place: 9 + 9 = 18. Write down 8, carry over 1..\n\nHundred millions place: 2 + 6 = 8, plus carryover 1 is 9. Write down 9..\n\nPutting all together:.\n\nHundred millions place: 9.\n\nTen millions: 8.\n\nMillions: 2.\n\nHundred thousands: 0.\n\nTen thousands: 1.\n\nThousands: 5.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nTens:7.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nWait, let me check again. Wait, after the millions place, the next digits are hundred thousands, ten thousands, thousands, etc. Wait, no. Let me actually break down each digit position properly..\n\nWait, perhaps I confused the places. Let me list each digit position from right to left (ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions, ten millions, hundred millions, billions). But since both numbers are 9-digit numbers, the highest place is hundred millions..\n\nLet's list each digit position for both numbers:.\n\nFirst number: 290,279,142.\n\nDigits (from right to left):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 2.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):4.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):1.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):9.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):7.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):2.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):0.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):9.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):2.\n\nSecond number:691,370,036.\n\nDigits:.\n\nPosition 1:6.\n\nPosition 2:3.\n\nPosition 3:0.\n\nPosition 4:0.\n\nPosition 5:7.\n\nPosition 6:3.\n\nPosition 7:1.\n\nPosition 8:9.\n\nPosition 9:6.\n\nWait, no. Let's write each number's digits correctly. Let's take 691,370,036..\n\nBreaking it down:.\n\nFrom right to left (positions 1 to 9):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones):6.\n\nPosition 2 (tens):3.\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):0.\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):0.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):7.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):3.\n\nPosition 7 (millions):1.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):9.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):6.\n\nWait, wait, 691,370,036 is 6 hundred millions, 9 ten millions, 1 million, 3 hundred thousands, 7 ten thousands, 0 thousands, 0 hundreds, 3 tens, 6 ones. So yes, positions:.\n\n9:6.\n\n8:9.\n\n7:1.\n\n6:3.\n\n5:7.\n\n4:0.\n\n3:0.\n\n2:3.\n\n1:6.\n\nSimilarly, 290,279,142 is 2 hundred millions, 9 ten millions, 0 millions, 2 hundred thousands, 7 ten thousands, 9 thousands, 1 hundred, 4 tens, 2 ones..\n\nSo positions:.\n\n9:2.\n\n8:9.\n\n7:0.\n\n6:2.\n\n5:7.\n\n4:9.\n\n3:1.\n\n2:4.\n\n1:2.\n\nNow adding each position from 1 to 9, with carryover:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 2 + 6 = 8. Write 8. Carryover 0..\n\nPosition 2 (tens):4 +3=7. Write7. Carryover 0..\n\nPosition3 (hundreds):1 +0=1. Write1. Carryover0..\n\nPosition4 (thousands):9 +0=9. Write9. Carryover0..\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):7 +7=14. Write4. Carryover1..\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):2 +3=5. Plus carryover1=6. Write6. Carryover0..\n\nPosition7 (millions):0 +1=1. Write1. Carryover0..\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):9 