\n- 9 (ten millions).\n- 7 (millions).\n- 1 (hundred thousands).\n- 6 (ten thousands).\n- 1 (thousands).\n- 2 (hundreds).\n- 2 (tens).\n- 0 (ones).\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake earlier. Let me confirm each digit's place..\n\nWait, maybe I need to break down both numbers properly to avoid confusion..\n\nFirst number: 197,161,220.\nDigits (from right to left):.\n0 (ones).\n2 (tens).\n2 (hundreds).\n1 (thousands).\n6 (ten thousands).\n1 (hundred thousands).\n7 (millions).\n9 (ten millions).\n1 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 800,090,976.\nDigits (from right to left):.\n6 (ones).\n7 (tens).\n9 (hundreds).\n0 (thousands).\n9 (ten thousands).\n0 (hundred thousands).\n0 (millions).\n0 (ten millions).\n8 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, that can't be right. Let me check again. Wait, when writing numbers, the rightmost digit is ones, then tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions, ten millions, hundred millions, etc..\n\nSo for 197,161,220:.\n\nDigits (right to left):.\nPosition 1 (ones): 0.\nPosition 2 (tens): 2.\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 2.\nPosition 4 (thousands): 1.\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 6.\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 1.\nPosition 7 (millions): 7.\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 9.\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 1.\n\nFor 800,090,976:.\n\nDigits (right to left):.\nPosition 1: 6.\nPosition 2: 7.\nPosition 3: 9.\nPosition 4: 0.\nPosition 5: 9.\nPosition 6: 0.\nPosition 7: 0.\nPosition 8: 0.\nPosition 9: 8.\n\nSo aligning them:.\n\nHundred millions (9): 1 vs 8.\nTen millions (8): 9 vs 0.\nMillions (7): 7 vs 0.\nHundred thousands (6): 1 vs 0.\nTen thousands (5): 6 vs 9.\nThousands (4): 1 vs 0.\nHundreds (3): 2 vs 9.\nTens (2): 2 vs 7.\nOnes (1): 0 vs 6.\n\nNow, adding each position starting from ones:.\n\nOnes: 0 + 6 = 6. Write down 6. No carry..\n\nTens: 2 +7 =9. Write 9. No carry..\n\nHundreds: 2 +9 =11. Write 1, carry over 1..\n\nThousands: 1 +0 =1, plus carry 1 =2. Write 2. No carry..\n\nTen thousands:6 +9=15. Write 5, carry 1..\n\nHundred thousands:1 +0=1 +1 (carry) =2. Write 2. No carry..\n\nMillions:7 +0=7. Write 7. No carry..\n\nTen millions:9 +0=9. Write 9. No carry..\n\nHundred millions:1 +8=9. Write 9..\n\nSo putting all together:.\n\nFrom ones to hundred millions:.\n\nOnes:6.\n\nTens:9.\n\nHundreds:1 (carry 1).\n\nThousands:2.\n\nTen thousands:5 (carry 1).\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nTen millions:9.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nWait, but wait, when adding the digits in each position:.\n\nWait, let's construct the sum step by step..\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones place: 0 + 6 = 6. Sum digit: 6. Carry: 0..\n\n2. Tens place: 2 + 7 =9. Sum digit:9. Carry:0..\n\n3. Hundreds place:2 +9=11. Sum digit:1. Carry:1..\n\n4. Thousands place:1 (from first number) +0 (from second) +1 (carry) =2. Sum digit:2. Carry:0..\n\n5. Ten thousands place:6 (first) +9 (second) =15. Sum digit:5. Carry:1..\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:1 (first) +0 (second) +1 (carry)=2. Sum digit:2. Carry:0..\n\n7. Millions place:7 (first) +0 (second) =7. Sum digit:7. Carry:0..\n\n8. Ten millions place:9 (first) +0 (second)=9. Sum digit:9. Carry:0..\n\n9. Hundred millions place:1 (first) +8 (second)=9. Sum digit:9. Carry:0..\n\nPutting all the digits together from hundred millions to ones:.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nTen millions:9.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nTen thousands:5.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nHundreds:1.\n\nTens:9.\n\nOnes:6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 29%|##9       | 145/500 [07:47<21:06,  3.57s/it] 29%|##9       | 146/500 [07:50<19:12,  3.26s/it]
