ry 1..\n5. Ten thousands: 3 + 2 = 5 + 1 (carry) = 6 → 6, carry 0..\n6. Hundred thousands: 6 + 7 = 13 → 3, carry 1..\n7. Millions: 3 + 7 = 10 + 1 (carry) = 11 → 1, carry 1..\n8. Ten millions: 6 + 3 = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10 → 0, carry 1..\n9. Hundred millions: 8 + 6 = 14 + 1 (carry) = 15 → 5, carry 1..\n10. Billions place: 0 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 1..\n\nSo putting it all together, the sum is 1,503,365,930. Wait, let me assemble the digits properly:.\n\nFrom billions to ones:.\n\n1 (billions), 5 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 3 (millions?), wait no. Wait, let me list the digits in order:.\n\nAfter adding:.\n\n- Billions: 1.\n- Hundred millions: 5.\n- Ten millions: 0.\n- Millions: 1.\n- Hundred thousands: 3.\n- Ten thousands: 6.\n- Thousands: 5.\n- Hundreds: 9.\n- Tens: 3.\n- Ones: 0.\n\nWait, but the millions place was obtained from adding the millions digits: 3 (from first number) and 7 (from second number) plus carry 1, totaling 11. So that's 1 in the millions place and carryover 1. Wait, but the millions place is the seventh digit from the right. Let's structure the number properly..\n\nWait, perhaps I should write each digit position as per their place:.\n\nThe sum is:.\n\n1 (billions).\n5 (hundred millions).\n0 (ten millions).\n3 (millions).\n3 (hundred thousands).\n6 (ten thousands).\n5 (thousands).\n9 (hundreds).\n3 (tens).\n0 (ones).\n\nWait, no. Let me check each step again carefully. Maybe I confused the positions. Let's list each digit position from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 0.\nPosition 2 (tens): 3.\nPosition 3 (hundreds):9.\nPosition 4 (thousands):5.\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):6.\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):3.\nPosition 7 (millions):1.\nPosition 8 (ten millions):0.\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):5.\nPosition 10 (billions):1.\n\nSo when we write the number from left to right (highest to lowest place), it's:.\n\n1 (billions), 5 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 6 (ten thousan