n starting from ones:.\n\nOnes place: 5 (from first number) +7 (second) =12. Write 2, carry 1..\n\nTens place:1 (from first) +6 (second) + carry 1=8. Write 8, no carry..\n\nHundreds place:5 (first) +1 (second)=6. Write 6..\n\nThousands place:2 (first) +1 (second)=3. Write 3..\n\nTen thousands place:6 (first) +8 (second)=14. Write 4, carry 1..\n\nHundred thousands place:5 (first) +0 (second) + carry 1=6. Write 6..\n\nMillions place:7 (first) +6 (second)=13. Write 3, carry 1..\n\nTen millions place:1 (first) +5 (second) + carry 1=7. Write 7..\n\nHundred millions place:2 (first) +9 (second)=11. Write 11</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
