ions place: The digits are 4 and 1. 4 + 1 = 5, plus the carryover 1 makes 6. So 6 goes here, no carryover..\n\nTen millions place: The digits are 2 and 7. 2 + 7 = 9. No carryover here..\n\nHundred millions place: The digits are 9 and 6. 9 + 6 = 15. Since there are no more digits to the left, we just write 15 here</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
