it, but let me verify each digit again carefully. Let's break down both numbers into their digits:.\n\nFirst number: 111,667,846.\n\nDigits from right to left (starting at ones place):.\n6 (ones).\n4 (tens).\n8 (hundreds).\n7 (thousands).\n6 (ten-thousands).\n6 (hundred-thousands).\n1 (millions).\n1 (ten-millions).\n1 (hundred-millions).\n\nSecond number:524,890,854.\n\nDigits from right to left:.\n4 (ones).\n5 (tens).\n8 (hundreds).\n0 (thousands).\n9 (ten-thousands).\n8 (hundred-thousands).\n4 (millions).\n2 (ten-millions).\n5 (hundred-millions).\n\nNow adding each corresponding digit with carryover:.\n\n1. Ones: 6 +4 =10 →0, carry 1..\n2. Tens:4 +5 =9 +1=10 →0, carry1..\n3. Hundreds:8 +8=16 +1=17 →7, carry1..\n4. Thousands:7 +0=7 +1=8 →8, carry0..\n5. Ten-thousands:6 +9=15 →5, carry1..\n6. Hundred-thousands:6 +8=14 +1=15 →5, carry1..\n7. Millions:1 +4=5 +1=6 →6, carry0..\n8. Ten-millions:1 +2=3 →3, carry0..\n9. Hundred-millions:1 +5=6 →6..\n\nPutting all digits together from the results:.\n\nHundred-millions:6.\nTen-millions:3.\nMillions:6.\nHundred-thousands:5.\nTen-thousands:5.\nThousands:8.\nHundreds:7.\nTens:0.\nOnes:0</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
