 3 + 1 = 4. So millions place is 4..\n\nNext up is the ten-millions place. The digits are 9 and 1. 9 + 1 = 10. So we put 0 here and carry over 1 to the hundred-millions place..\n\nFinally, the hundred-millions place. The digits are 5 and 4. Adding them plus the carry-over: 5 + 4 + 1 = 10. So we write 0 here and carry over 1, but since there are no more digits left, that carry-over becomes a new digit at the front</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
