      + 9 2 7 3 4 2 9 2 7.\n        -------------------.\n\nBut perhaps writing each digit position by position:.\n\nOnes place: 3 + 7 = 10. So we write 0, carry over 1..\n\nTens place: 2 + 2 = 4, plus the carried 1 makes 5. No carry-over here..\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 9 = 16. Write down 6, carry over 1..\n\nThousands place: 8 + 2 = 10, plus the carry 1 makes 11. Write 1, carry over 1..\n\nTen thousands place: 0 + 4 = 4, plus carry 1 makes 5. No carry..\n\nHundred thousands place: 2 + 3 = 5. No carry..\n\nMillions place: 3 + 7 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1..\n\nTen millions place: 1 + 2 = 3, plus carry 1 makes 4..\n\nHundred millions place: 1 + 9 = 10. Write 0, carry over 1. But since there are no higher places, that carry becomes a new digit at the beginning..\n\nPutting all together, the sum would be 1 (from the final carry) followed by the digits from hundred millions down: 0 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (ones). Wait, let me check again..\n\nWait, let me go step by step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones place: 3 +7 =10 → 0, carry 1..\n\n2. Tens place: 2 +2=4 +1=5 → 5, carry 0..\n\n3. Hundreds place:7 +9=16 →6, carry 1..\n\n4. Thousands place:8 +2=10 +1=11 →1, carry 1..\n\n5. Ten thousands place:0 +4=4 +1=5 →5, carry 0..\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:2 +3=5 →5, carry 0..\n\n7. Millions place:3 +7=10 →0, carry 1..\n\n8. Ten millions place:1 +2=3 +1=4 →4, carry 0..\n\n9. Hundred millions place:1 +9=10 →0, carry 1..\n\nNow, after adding all digits, we have a carry of 1 left, which becomes the next digit. So the sum is 1 followed by the results from each step in reverse order (since we added from right to left). Wait, no, actually, the digits are added starting from the right, so the first digit we computed (ones) is the rightmost digit of the result. The carry at the end (from hundred millions place) becomes the leftmost digit..\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nThe digits from right to left (ones to hundred millions) are:.\n\n0 (ones), 5 (tens), 6 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 5 (hundred thousands), 0 (millions), 4 (ten millions), 0 (hundred millions), and then the carryover 1 (billions place)..\n\nWait, but the original numbers are 9-digit numbers, so adding them could result in a 10-digit number. So the final sum would be:.\n\n1 (billions place), 0 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 5 (tens), 0 (ones)..\n\nWait, let me verify that. Let's write each digit position:.\n\nAfter adding:.\n\n- Ones: 0.\n\n- Tens:5.\n\n- Hundreds:6.\n\n- Thousands:1.\n\n- Ten thousands:5.\n\n- Hundred thousands:5.\n\n- Millions:0 (from 3+7=10, carry 1, but wait, millions place was 3 from first number and 7 from second number? Wait, the first number is 113,208,723. Breaking down:.\n\nDigits of first number (113,208,723):.\n\nHundred millions:1.\n\nTen millions:1.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nTen thousands:0.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nTens:2.\n\nOnes:3.\n\nSecond number (927,342,927):.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nTen millions:2.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nHundred thousands:3.\n\nTen thousands:4.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nTens:2.\n\nOnes:7.\n\nSo when adding each position:.\n\n1. Ones: 3 +7 =10 →0, carry 1..\n\n2. Tens:2 +2=4 +1=5 →5, carry 0..\n\n3. Hundreds:7 +9=16 →6, carry1..\n\n4. Thousands:8 +2=10 +1=11 →1, carry1..\n\n5. Ten thousands:0 +4=4 +1=5 →5, carry0..\n\n6. Hundred thousands:2 +3=5 →5, carry0..\n\n7. Millions:3 +7=10 →0, carry1..\n\n8. Ten millions:1 +2=3 +1=4 →4, carry0..\n\n9. Hundred millions:1 +9=10 →0, carry1..\n\nThen, the carry1 from hundred millions place is added as the next digit (billions place:1)..\n\nSo the sum is 1 (billions), 0 (hundred millions),4 (ten millions),0 (millions),5 (hundred thousands),5 (ten thousands),1 (thousands),6 (hundreds),5 (tens),0 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 34%|###3      | 168/500 [08:49<14:16,  2.58s/it]
