messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 172741420 and 629034794?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let's tackle adding 172,741,420 and 629,034,794. Hmm, starting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. Let's line them up properly:.\n\n172,741,420.\n+629,034,794.\n-------------.\n\nStarting with the ones place: 0 + 4 = 4. So the ones digit is 4. No carry-over there..\n\nNext, tens place: 2 + 9 = 11. Oh, wait, the second number's tens digit is 9 (from 794), and the first number's tens digit is 2 (from 420). Adding those gives 11. So we write down 1 in the tens place and carry over 1 to the hundreds place..\n\nHundreds place: 4 (from 420) + 7 (from 794) plus the carried 1 equals 12. So that's 2 in the hundreds place with a carry of 1..\n\nMoving to the thousands place: 1 (from 741,420) + 3 (from 034,794) plus the carry 1. Wait, let me check the digits again. The first number here is 172,741,420, so breaking it down:.\n\nDigits (from right):.\n0 (ones), 2 (tens), 4 (hundreds), 1 (thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 7 (hundred thousands), 2 (millions), 7 (ten millions), 1 (hundred millions)..\n\nWait, maybe I should write both numbers aligned:.\n\n       1 7 2 7 4 1 4 2 0.\n    + 6 2 9 0 3 4 7 9 4.\n    -------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\n0 + 4 = 4 (ones).\n2 + 9 = 11 (tens: 1, carry 1).\n4 + 7 + 1 = 12 (hundreds: 2, carry 1).\n1 + 4 = 5 + 1 (carry?) Wait, maybe I'm mixing up the places. Let me write each digit position properly..\n\nLet's break down each number into their digits from ones to higher places:.\n\nFirst number (172,741,420):.\n- Ones: 0.\n- Tens: 2.\n- Hundreds: 4.\n- Thousands: 1.\n- Ten thousands: 4.\n- Hundred thousands: 7.\n- Millions: 2.\n- Ten millions: 7.\n- Hundred millions: 1.\n\nSecond number (629,034,794):.\n- Ones: 4.\n- Tens: 9.\n- Hundreds: 7.\n- Thousands: 4.\n- Ten thousands: 3.\n- Hundred thousands: 0.\n- Millions: 9.\n- Ten millions: 2.\n- Hundred millions: 6.\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nOnes: 0 + 4 = 4.\nTens: 2 + 9 = 11 → 1 in tens place, carryover 1.\nHundreds: 4 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 12 → 2 in hundreds, carry 1.\nThousands: 1 (from first) + 4 (from second) + 1 (carry) = 6 → carry 0.\nTen thousands: 4 (first) + 3 (second) = 7 → carry 0.\nHundred thousands: 7 (first) + 0 (second) = 7 → carry 0.\nMillions: 2 (first) + 9 (second) = 11 → 1 in millions, carry 1.\nTen millions: 7 (first) + 2 (second) + 1 (carry) = 10 → 0 in ten millions, carry 1.\nHundred millions: 1 (first) + 6 (second) + 1 (carry) = 8.\n\nPutting it all together from the highest digit to the lowest:.\n\n8 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 4 (ones). Wait, but let me check again:.\n\nWait, after adding hundred millions: 1 +6 +1=8..\n\nTen millions: 7 +2 +1 (carry from millions) =10 → so 0 here and carry 1 to hundred millions. But we already added that. Wait, perhaps I made a mistake in the order..\n\nLet me redo the steps carefully:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n1. Ones: 0 +4 =4. Sum:4. Carry:0..\n\n2. Tens: 2 +9=11. Sum:1 (tens place). Carry:1..\n\n3. Hundreds:4 +7=11 +1 (carry)=12. Sum:2 (hundreds). Carry:1..\n\n4. Thousands:1 (from first number) +4 (from second) +1 (carry)=6. Sum:6. Carry:0..\n\n5. Ten thousands:4 +3=7. Sum:7. Carry:0..\n\n6. Hundred thousands:7 +0=7. Sum:7. Carry:0..\n\n7. Millions:2 +9=11. Sum:1 (millions). Carry:1..\n\n8. Ten millions:7 +2=9 +1 (carry)=10. Sum:0 (ten millions). Carry:1..\n\n9. Hundred millions:1 (from first) +6 (from second) +1 (carry)=8. Sum:8. Carry:0..\n\nSo combining all the digits from hundred millions to ones:.\n\n8 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 7 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 4 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 37%|###7      | 186/500 [09:40<13:58,  2.67s/it]
