 place: 7 (from first number) + 1 (from second) = 8, plus the carryover 1 makes 9. So that's 9, no carryover..\n\nHundred millions place: 8 (from first) + 4 (from second) = 12. So 2 here with a carryover of 1. But since there are no more digits beyond that, we add the carryover. So the final digits would be 1 (carryover) followed by 2, then the rest as calculated..\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 11 → 1, carry 1.\n\nTens: 6 + 6 = 12 +1 =13 →3, carry1.\n\nHundreds:4 +7=11 +1=12 →2, carry1.\n\nThousands:1 +6=7 +1=8 →8, no carry.\n\nTen thousands:0 +4=4 →4.\n\nHundred thousands:0 +2=2 →2.\n\nMillions:7 +8=15 →5, carry1.\n\nTen millions:7 +1=8 +1=9 →9.\n\nHundred millions:8 +4=12 →2, carry1.\n\nThen the carryover 1 at the hundred millions place becomes the billions place, which is 1..\n\nSo putting all digits together from left to right: 1 (billions), 2 (hundred millions),9 (ten millions),5 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),2 (hundreds),3 (tens),1 (ones)..\n\nWait, let me check again:.\n\nWait, when we add the hundred millions place: 8 (from first number) +4 (from second) =12. So write 2, carryover 1. Then the next higher place (billions) is just the carryover 1..\n\nSo the full number would be 1,2 (hundred millions),9 (ten millions),5 (millions),2 (hundred thousands),4 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),2 (hundreds),3 (tens),1 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
