nPosition 7 (millions): 4 + 9 = 13. Write down 3, carry over 1..\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 8 + 7 = 15, plus carryover 1 = 16. Write down 6, carry over 1..\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 5 + 2 = 7, plus carryover 1 = 8. Write down 8..\n\nSo putting all the digits together from position 9 to 1:.\n\nHundred millions: 8.\nTen millions: 6.\nMillions: 3.\nHundred thousands:8.\nTen thousands:8.\nThousands:6.\nHundreds:0.\nTens:3.\nOnes:8.\n\nWait, but let's check the order. When we put the digits together, starting from the highest place (hundred millions) to the ones, the sum would be:.\n\nHundred millions:8.\nTen millions:6.\nMillions:3.\nHundred thousands:8.\nTen thousands:8.\nThousands:6.\nHundreds:0.\nTens:3.\nOnes:8</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 40%|###9      | 198/500 [10:16<16:22,  3.25s/it]
