it, so when adding the millions place: the first number has 2 in the millions place (from 852,989,335), and the second number has 0 in the millions place (from 890,722,935). So 2 + 0 = 2, plus the carryover 1 from the previous step (hundred-thousands place), which was 17, so we carried 1. So 2 + 0 +1 =3. So millions place is 3, no carryover here. .\n\nThen, **Ten millions place:** 5 (from first number) +9 (from second number) =14. Write down 4, carry over 1..\n\n**Hundred millions place:** 8 +8 =16, plus the carried 1 makes 17. So write down 7, carry over 1. But since there are no more digits beyond the hundred millions place, we add that carry as a new digit to the left. So the final sum would start with 1 followed by 7 in the hundred millions place..\n\nPutting all the digits together from each step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:0.\n\nTens:7.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nTen-thousands:1.\n\nHundred-thousands:7.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nTen-millions:4.\n\nHundred-millions:7.\n\nPlus the carried 1 at the very left: 1.\n\nWait, let me list the digits in order:.\n\nFrom the largest place to smallest:.\n\nThe carried over 1 (billion place), then 7 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 0 (ones)..\n\nWait, I think I might have mixed up some places. Let me reconstruct the sum properly..\n\nLet me do the addition step by step again more carefully..\n\nWriting both numbers:.\n\n          8 5 2 9 8 9 3 3 5.\n        +8 9 0 7 2 2 9 3 5.\n        --------------------.\n\nAdding each column from right to left:.\n\n1. Ones: 5 +5 =10 → 0, carry 1.\n2. Tens:3 +3=6 +1=7 →7, carry 0.\n3. Hundreds:3 +9=12 →2, carry 1.\n4. Thousands:9 +2=11 +1=12 →2, carry1.\n5. Ten thousands:8 +2=10 +1=11 →1, carry1.\n6. Hundred thousands:9 +7=16 +1=17 →7, carry1.\n7. Millions:2 +0=2 +1=3 →3, carry0.\n8. Ten millions:5 +9=14 →4, carry1.\n9. Hundred millions:8 +8=16 +1=17 →7, carry1.\n10. Then, there's no higher place, so the carry 1 becomes a new digit at the left:1..\n\nSo putting it all together, starting from the leftmost digit (the billion place):.\n\n1 (from the final carry) followed by 7 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 7 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 0 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 40%|###9      | 199/500 [10:19<15:29,  3.09s/it]
