are no higher places, we write 14 as 4 and 1 in the next higher place (billions place)..\n\nSo putting all together:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\nPosition1:2.\n\nPosition2:4.\n\nPosition3:5.\n\nPosition4:2 (with carryover1).\n\nPosition5:3.\n\nPosition6:3.\n\nPosition7:7.\n\nPosition8:6.\n\nPosition9:4 (from 6+8=14, write 4 carry 1).\n\nThen the carryover1 becomes the billions place digit:1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 41%|####      | 203/500 [10:29<13:38,  2.76s/it] 41%|####      | 204/500 [10:32<13:16,  2.69s/it]
