the right (ones place):.\n\n6 (ones) + 9 = 15 → 5, carry 1  .\n6 (tens) +4 =10 +1 =11 →1, carry1  .\n7 (hundreds) +5=12 +1=13 →3, carry1  .\n8 (thousands) +3=11 +1=12 →2, carry1  .\n2 (ten thousands) +4=6 +1=7 →7, carry0  .\n3 (hundred thousands) +9=12 →2, carry1  .\n6 (millions) +7=13 +1=14 →4, carry1  .\n3 (ten millions) +2=5 +1=6 →6, carry0  .\n4 (hundred millions) +5=9 →9..\n\nWait, so putting all together from right to left:.\n\nOnes:5  .\nTens:1  .\nHundreds:3  .\nThousands:2  .\nTen thousands:7  .\nHundred thousands:2  .\nMillions:4  .\nTen millions:6  .\nHundred millions:9..\n\nWait, but the second number is 527,945,349. Let me check each digit position again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits..\n\nFirst number: 436,382,766  .\nDigits (from right to left):  .\nPosition 1 (ones):6  .\nPosition2 (tens):6  .\nPosition3 (hundreds):7  .\nPosition4 (thousands):2  .\nPosition5 (ten thousands):8  .\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):3  .\nPosition7 (millions):6  .\nPosition8 (ten millions):3  .\nPosition9 (hundred millions):4  .\n\nSecond number:527,945,349  .\nDigits (from right to left):  .\nPosition1:9  .\nPosition2:4  .\nPosition3:5  .\nPosition4:3  .\nPosition5:4  .\nPosition6:9  .\nPosition7:7  .\nPosition8:2  .\nPosition9:5  .\n\nSo adding position by position:.\n\n1. Ones:6+9=15 →5, carry1  .\n2. Tens:6+4=10 +1=11 →1, carry1  .\n3. Hundreds:7+5=12 +1=13 →3, carry1  .\n4. Thousands:2+3=5 +1=6 →6, carry0  .\nWait wait! Wait, in the thousands place: first number has 2 (since 436,382,766 is 4 3 6, 3 8 2, 7 6 6. Wait, maybe I messed up the digit positions. Let me confirm:.\n\nBreaking down 436,382,766:  .\nHundred millions:4  .\nTen millions:3  .\nMillions:6  .\nHundred thousands:3  .\nTen thousands:8  .\nThousands:2  .\nHundreds:7  .\nTens:6  .\nOnes:6  .\n\nWait, no, that's not right. Wait 436,382,766 is structured as:.\n\n4 (hundred million)  .\n3 (ten million)  .\n6 (million)  .\n3 (hundred thousand)  .\n8 (ten thousand)  .\n2 (thousand)  .\n7 (hundred)  .\n6 (ten)  .\n6 (one)  .\n\nSimilarly, 527,945,349:  .\n5 (hundred million)  .\n2 (ten million)  .\n7 (million)  .\n9 (hundred thousand)  .\n4 (ten thousand)  .\n5 (thousand)  .\n3 (hundred)  .\n4 (ten)  .\n9 (one)  .\n\nSo when adding digit by digit:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes:6 +9=15 →5, carry1  .\nTens:6 +4=10 +1=11 →1, carry1  .\nHundreds:7 +3=10 +1=11 →1, carry1  .\nThousands:2 +5=7 +1=8 →8, carry0  .\nTen thousands:8 +4=12 →2, carry1  .\nHundred thousands:3 +9=12 +1=13 →3, carry1  .\nMillions:6 +7=13 +1=14 →4, carry1  .\nTen millions:3 +2=5 +1=6 →6, carry0  .\nHundred millions:4 +5=9 →9.  .\n\nWait, but earlier I thought the thousands place was 2+3=5 +1=6. But according to this breakdown, thousands place is first number's 2 vs second number's 5 (since 527,945,349's thousands place is 5). Wait, that's where I made a mistake earlier. Let me correct:.\n\nFirst number's thousands digit is 2 (as in 436,382,766: the thousands digit is the 2 in the ...,382,766). The second number's thousands digit is 5 (from 527,945,349: the thousands digit is the 5 in ...45,349). So thousands place is 2 +5=7. But earlier I thought it was 2 +3, which was wrong. So this is a mistake..\n\nSo correcting:.\n\nThousands place: 2 (from first number) +5 (from second number) =7. Plus any carry-over from the hundreds place. The hundreds place added to 7+3=10, which gave a carry of 1. Wait, in the hundreds place, we have 7 (from first number) and 3 (from second number). So 7+3=10, plus the carry-over 1 from the tens place (which was 11). So total 10 +1=11. So hundreds place is 1, carry 1. Then thousands place: 2+5=7, plus the carry-over 1 from hundreds place? Wait no. Let's step through again:.\n\nOnes:6+9=15 →5, carry1  .\nTens:6+4=10 +1=11 →1, carry1  .\nHundreds:7+3=10 +1=11 →1, carry1  .\nThousands:2+5=7 +1 (carry from hundreds) →8, carry0  .\nTen thousands:8+4=12 +0 (no carry) →2, carry1  .\nHundred thousands:3+9=12 +1=13 →3, carry1  .\nMillions:6+7=13 +1=14 →4, carry1  .\nTen millions:3+2=5 +1=6 →6, carry0  .\nHundred millions:4+5=9..\n\nSo the digits from right to left (after addition) are:.\n\nOnes:5  .\nTens:1  .\nHundreds:1  .\nThousands:8  .\nTen thousands:2  .\nHundred thousands:3  .\nMillions:4  .\nTen millions:6  .\nHundred millions:9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 43%|####2     | 214/500 [11:04<14:18,  3.00s/it]
