 =9. Write 9, no carryover..\n\nHundreds place:9 +5=14. Write 4, carryover 1..\n\nThousands place:3 +3=6 +1=7. Write 7, no carryover..\n\nTen thousands place:3 +1=4. Write 4..\n\nHundred thousands place:3 +1=4. Write 4..\n\nMillions place:0 +6=6. Write 6..\n\nTen millions place:7 +1=8. Write 8..\n\nHundred millions place:9 +2=11. Write 1 and carryover 1, but since there are no more digits, that carryover becomes a new digit at the beginning. Wait, but in the original numbers, the first number has 9 in hundred millions and the second has 2, so adding 9 +2=11. So the hundred millions place is 1 and carryover 1 to the next place, which is billions. So the billions place would be 1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
