messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 313544986 and 595618793?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let's see. I need to add 313,544,986 and 595,618,793. Hmm, starting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place..\n\nFirst, the ones digits: 6 and 3. Adding those gives 9. Okay, so ones place is 9..\n\nNext, the tens place: 8 and 9. Wait, 8 plus 9 is 17. So I write down 7 and carry over 1 to the next column..\n\nHundreds place: 9 and 7. But don't forget the carried-over 1. So 9 + 7 = 16, plus 1 is 17. Again, write 7 and carry 1..\n\nThousands place: 4 and 8. Plus the carry 1. 4 + 8 = 12, plus 1 is 13. So 3 here, carry 1..\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 and 1. Wait, wait, let's make sure the digits line up correctly. The first number is 313,544,986. Breaking it down:.\n\nDigits from right:.\n6 (ones),.\n8 (tens),.\n9 (hundreds),.\n4 (thousands),.\n4 (ten thousands),.\n5 (hundred thousands),.\n3 (millions),.\n1 (ten millions),.\n3 (hundred millions)..\n\nSecond number 595,618,793:.\n\n3 (ones),.\n9 (tens),.\n7 (hundreds),.\n8 (thousands),.\n1 (ten thousands),.\n6 (hundred thousands),.\n8 (millions),.\n5 (ten millions),.\n9 (hundred millions)..\n\nWait, maybe I should write them aligned:.\n\n313,544,986.\n595,618,793.\n\nLet me list each digit position by position:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 6 + 3 = 9.\nPosition 2 (tens): 8 + 9 = 17 (carry 1).\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 9 + 7 + 1 = 17 (carry 1).\nPosition 4 (thousands): 4 + 8 + 1 = 13 (carry 1).\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 4 + 1 +1 = 6.\nWait, wait. Let's check the positions again carefully..\n\nWait, 313,544,986 is:.\n\n3 1 3 5 4 4 9 8 6.\n\nBut wait, numbers are:.\n\n313,544,986:.\n\nBreak into digits:.\n\n3 (hundred millions).\n1 (ten millions).\n3 (millions).\n5 (hundred thousands).\n4 (ten thousands).\n4 (thousands).\n9 (hundreds).\n8 (tens).\n6 (ones).\n\nAnd 595,618,793:.\n\n5 (hundred millions).\n9 (ten millions).\n5 (millions).\n6 (hundred thousands).\n1 (ten thousands).\n8 (thousands).\n7 (hundreds).\n9 (tens).\n3 (ones).\n\nWait, maybe I should align them properly:.\n\n313,544,986: positions from right (ones to hundred millions):.\n\n6 (1st digit - ones).\n8 (2nd - tens).\n9 (3rd - hundreds).\n4 (4th - thousands).\n4 (5th - ten thousands).\n5 (6th - hundred thousands).\n3 (7th - millions).\n1 (8th - ten millions).\n3 (9th - hundred millions).\n\n595,618,793:.\n\n3 (1st).\n9 (2nd).\n7 (3rd).\n8 (4th).\n1 (5th).\n6 (6th).\n5 (7th).\n9 (8th).\n5 (9th).\n\nSo when adding, each corresponding digit:.\n\n1st (ones): 6 +3 =9.\n\n2nd (tens):8 +9=17, write 7, carry 1.\n\n3rd (hundreds):9 +7=16, plus carry 1=17, write 7, carry 1.\n\n4th (thousands):4 +8=12, plus carry 1=13, write 3, carry 1.\n\n5th (ten thousands):4 +1=5, plus carry 1=6, write 6, carry 0.\n\n6th (hundred thousands):5 +6=11, write 1, carry 1.\n\n7th (millions):3 +5=8, plus carry 1=9, write 9, carry 0.\n\n8th (ten millions):1 +9=10, write 0, carry 1.\n\n9th (hundred millions):3 +5=8, plus carry 1=9, write 9..\n\nWait, but let me check that again step by step..\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:.\n\n1. Ones place: 6 +3 =9. No carry. So digit1:9..\n\n2. Tens place:8 +9=17. So digit2:7, carryover 1..\n\n3. Hundreds place:9 +7=16, plus carry 1=17. So digit3:7, carryover 1..\n\n4. Thousands place:4 (from first number) +8 (second number) =12, plus carry 1=13. So digit4:3, carryover 1..\n\n5. Ten thousands place:4 (first) +1 (second) =5, plus carry 1=6. So digit5:6, carryover 0..\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:5 (first) +6 (second) =11. So digit6:1, carryover 1..\n\n7. Millions place:3 (first) +5 (second) =8, plus carryover 1=9. So digit7:9, carryover 0..\n\n8. Ten millions place:1 (first) +9 (second) =10. So digit8:0, carryover 1..\n\n9. Hundred millions place:3 (first) +5 (second) =8, plus carryover 1=9. So digit9:9</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 44%|####4     | 221/500 [11:23<12:29,  2.69s/it] 44%|####4     | 222/500 [11:25<12:38,  2.73s/it]
