ht as per place value:.\n\nBreaking down 667,325,620:.\n\nPosition (from left):.\n\n1. Hundred millions: 6.\n\n2. Ten millions: 6.\n\n3. Millions: 7.\n\n4. Hundred thousands:3.\n\n5. Ten thousands:2.\n\n6. Thousands:5.\n\n7. Hundreds:6.\n\n8. Tens:2.\n\n9. Ones:0.\n\nSimilarly, 571,128,998:.\n\n1. Hundred millions:5.\n\n2. Ten millions:7.\n\n3. Millions:1.\n\n4. Hundred thousands:1.\n\n5. Ten thousands:2.\n\n6. Thousands:8.\n\n7. Hundreds:9.\n\n8. Tens:9.\n\n9. Ones:8.\n\nSo when adding, the digits line up as:.\n\nHundred millions:6 +5.\n\nTen millions:6 +7.\n\nMillions:7 +1.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +1.\n\nTen thousands:2 +2.\n\nThousands:5 +8.\n\nHundreds:6 +9.\n\nTens:2 +9.\n\nOnes:0 +8.\n\nNow let's add each position starting from the ones:.\n\nOnes:0 +8=8 →8.\n\nTens:2+9=11 →1, carry 1.\n\nHundreds:6+9=15 +carry 1=16 →6, carry 1.\n\nThousands:5+8=13 +carry 1=14 →4, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands:2+2=4 +carry1=5 →5, no carry.\n\nHundred thousands:3+1=4 →4.\n\nMillions:7+1=8 →8.\n\nTen millions:6+7=13 →3, carry 1.\n\nHundred millions:6+5=11 +carry 1=12 →2, carry 1.\n\nWait, but now we have a carry-over of 1 after adding the hundred millions place. Since there's no higher place, we need to add that as a new digit to the left. So the total would be 1 (carry) followed by the hundred millions sum. So:.\n\nThe sum would be:.\n\n1 (from the final carry) 2 (hundred millions), then 3 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands),5 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),6 (hundreds),1 (tens),8 (ones)..\n\nWait, putting it all together:.\n\n1 (carry) then 2 (hundred millions) + 3 (ten millions) etc</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 53%|#####3    | 265/500 [13:33<11:40,  2.98s/it] 53%|#####3    | 266/500 [13:36<11:28,  2.94s/it]
