s) 1 (ones)..\n\nSecond number: 8 (hundred millions) 4 (ten millions) 6 (millions) 3 (hundred thousands) 0 (ten thousands) 5 (thousands) 2 (hundreds) 1 (tens) 5 (ones)..\n\nSo when adding the ten millions place: 5 (from first) + 4 (from second) plus any carry-over. Wait, earlier in the millions place, we had 5 + 6 = 11, which caused a carry-over of 1. So the ten millions place is 5 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 10. So we write 0 here and carry over 1 to the hundred millions place..\n\nNow the hundred millions place: 9 (from first) + 8 (from second) + 1 (carry-over) = 18. So we write 8 here and carry over 1. Wait, but 9 +8 is 17, plus 1 is 18. So the hundred millions digit is 8 and carry-over 1. But since there are no higher places, that carry-over becomes a new digit at the front. So the total would be 1,8xx,xxx,xxx..\n\nWait, let's go step by step again to make sure. Let me list each digit position with the addition:.\n\nOnes: 1 +5 =6. Sum digit:6. Carry:0..\n\nTens:8 +1=9. Sum:9. Carry:0..\n\nHundreds:8 +2=10. Sum:0. Carry:1..\n\nThousands:2 +5 +1 (carry)=8. Sum:8. Carry:0..\n\nTen thousands:4 +0=4. Sum:4. Carry:0..\n\nHundred thousands:6 +3=9. Sum:9. Carry:0..\n\nMillions:6 +6=12. Sum:2. Carry:1..\n\nTen millions:5 +4 +1=10. Sum:0. Carry:1..\n\nHundred millions:9 +8 +1=18. Sum:8. Carry:1..\n\nNow, since we have a carry-over of 1 after the hundred millions place, we add a new digit at the beginning: 1..\n\nSo putting all the digits together with the carry-over:.\n\n1 (from the final carry) 8 (hundred millions) 0 (ten millions) 2 (millions) 9 (hundred thousands) 4 (ten thousands) 8 (thousands) 0 (hundreds) 9 (tens) 6 (ones)..\n\nWait, let me check that again. Wait, the digits from each step:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:6.\n\nTens:9.\n\nHundreds:0 (with a carry-over of 1).\n\nThousands:8 (carry 0).\n\nTen thousands:4.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nMillions:2 (carry 1).\n\nTen millions:0 (carry 1).\n\nHundred millions:8 (carry 1).\n\nThen the final carry 1 becomes the next digit. So the sum is 1 (billion place), then 8 (hundred million), 0 (ten million), 2 (million), 9 (hundred thousand), 4 (ten thousand), 8 (thousand), 0 (hundred), 9 (ten), 6 (one)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 57%|#####6    | 285/500 [14:30<10:09,  2.83s/it]
