nfirm:.\n\nBreaking down 118,468,573:.\n\nPositions (from right to left):.\n3 (ones).\n7 (tens).\n5 (hundreds).\n8 (thousands).\n6 (ten thousands).\n4 (hundred thousands).\n8 (millions).\n1 (ten millions).\n1 (hundred millions).\n\nSo when adding vertically:.\n\nHundred millions: 6 (from first number) + 1 (from second) = 7.\nTen millions: 3 + 1 = 4.\nMillions: 6 + 8 = 14, carry over 1.\nHundred thousands:6 +4=10 plus carry 1=11, carry 1.\nTen thousands:5 +6=11 plus carry 1=12, carry 1.\nThousands:6 +8=14 plus carry 1=15, carry 1.\nHundreds:0 +5=5 plus carry 1=6.\nTens:8 +7=15, carry 1.\nOnes:0 +3=3 plus carry 1=4? Wait, no. Wait in the ones place, first number has 0, second has 3. So 0+3=3. Then tens place: 8+7=15. So carry 1 to hundreds place. Then hundreds: 0+5=5 plus 1 carried=6. Thousands place:6+8=14, plus carry 0 (since previous step didn't carry over after hundreds?), wait maybe I got confused here..\n\nWait let's do it step by step properly:.\n\nStart from the right:.\n\nOnes: 0 + 3 = 3. Write 3. No carry..\n\nTens: 8 + 7 = 15. Write 5, carry 1..\n\nHundreds: 0 + 5 = 5. Add carry 1: 6. Write 6. No carry..\n\nThousands: 6 + 8 = 14. Write 4, carry 1..\n\nTen thousands: 5 + 6 = 11. Add carry 1: 12. Write 2, carry 1..\n\nHundred thousands:6 +4=10. Add carry 1:11. Write 1, carry 1..\n\nMillions:6 +8=14. Add carry 1:15. Write 5, carry 1..\n\nTen millions:3 +1=4. Add carry 1:5. Write 5..\n\nHundred millions:6 +1=7. Write 7..\n\nSo combining all the digits from the highest place to lowest:.\n\n7 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions),5 (millions),1 (hundred thousands),2 (ten thousands),4 (thousands),6 (hundreds),5 (tens),3 (ones)..\n\nWait, but when we did the thousands place, it was 6 (from first number) +8 (from second) =14. So we write 4 there, carry 1. Then ten thousands place:5+6=11 plus carry 1 is 12. So yes, 2 and carry 1..\n\nHundred thousands place:6+4=10 plus carry 1=11, so 1 and carry 1..\n\nMillions place:6+8=14 plus carry 1=15. So 5, carry 1..\n\nTen millions:3+1=4 plus carry 1=5..\n\nHundred millions:6+1=7</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
