s:8.\n\nHundreds:5.\n\nThousands:0 (with a carry 1).\n\nTen-thousands:1 (with carry 1).\n\nHundred-thousands:2 (with carry 1).\n\nMillions:5 (with carry 1).\n\nTen-millions:3 (with carry 1).\n\nHundred-millions:3 (with carry 1).\n\nBut since after hundred-millions, there's a carry of 1 left, that becomes the next digit, which is billions place. So the final number would be 1,3,3,5,2,0,5,5,8,2. Let me check that again..\n\nWait, let's write each digit position properly:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 7 +5 =12 →2, carry 1..\n\nTens:0 +7 =7 +1=8 →8, carry 0..\n\nHundreds:1 +4=5 →5, carry 0..\n\nThousands:5 +5=10 →0, carry1..\n\nTen-thousands:7 +3=10 +1=11 →1, carry1..\n\nHundred-thousands:4 +7=11 +1=12 →2, carry1..\n\nMillions:7 +7=14 +1=15 →5, carry1..\n\nTen-millions:7 +5=12 +1=13 →3, carry1..\n\nHundred-millions:7 +5=12 +1=13 →3, carry1..\n\nThen, since there are no more digits to add, the carry1 goes to the next higher place, which is billions. So the digits are:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred-millions:3.\n\nTen-millions:3.\n\nMillions:5.\n\nHundred-thousands:2.\n\nTen-thousands:0.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nHundreds:5.\n\nTens:8.\n\nOnes:2.\n\nSo putting it all together: 1,3,3,5,2,0,5,5,8,2 → 1,335,205,582. Wait, let me format that with commas: 1,335,205,582..\n\nWait, but wait, let's verify with a calculator. Let me check 777,475,107 +557,735,475..\n\nCalculating:.\n\n777,475,107.\n\n+557,735,475.\n\n= ?.\n\nAdding them:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n7 +5=12 →2, carry1..\n\n0 +7=7 +1=8 →8..\n\n1 +4=5 →5..\n\n5 +5=10 →0, carry1..\n\n7 +3=10 +1=11 →1, carry1..\n\n4 +7=11 +1=12 →2, carry1..\n\n7 +7=14 +1=15 →5, carry1..\n\n7 +5=12 +1=13 →3, carry1..\n\n7 +5=12 +1=13 →3, carry1..\n\nFinally, the carry1 →1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 60%|#####9    | 298/500 [15:09<11:23,  3.38s/it]
