dred thousands).\n7: 2 (millions).\n8: 2 (ten millions).\n9: 1 (hundred millions).\n\nFor 537,011,818:.\n\nPosition:.\n1: 8 (ones).\n2: 1 (tens).\n3: 8 (hundreds).\n4: 1 (thousands).\n5: 1 (ten thousands).\n6: 0 (hundred thousands).\n7: 7 (millions).\n8: 3 (ten millions).\n9: 5 (hundred millions).\n\nNow, adding each position:.\n\nStarting from the ones place (position 1):.\n\n1. Ones place: 0 (from first number) + 8 (from second) = 8. Write down 8. No carry-over..\n\n2. Tens place: 0 + 1 = 1. Write down 1. No carry-over..\n\n3. Hundreds place: 4 + 8 = 12. Write down 2, carry over 1..\n\n4. Thousands place: 8 + 1 = 9, plus the carried 1 makes 10. Write down 0, carry over 1..\n\n5. Ten thousands place: 0 + 1 = 1, plus carry 1 makes 2. Write down 2. No carry-over..\n\n6. Hundred thousands place: 3 + 0 = 3. Write down 3. No carry-over..\n\n7. Millions place: 2 + 7 = 9. Write down 9. No carry-over..\n\n8. Ten millions place: 2 + 3 = 5. Write down 5. No carry-over..\n\n9. Hundred millions place: 1 + 5 = 6. Write down 6..\n\nPutting all the digits together from the highest place to the lowest:.\n\n6 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 9 (millions), 3 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 8 (ones). Wait, let's check that again..\n\nWait, let's reconstruct the sum step by step:.\n\nAfter adding each digit:.\n\nHundred millions place: 1 + 5 = 6.\n\nTen millions: 2 + 3 = 5.\n\nMillions: 2 +7 =9.\n\nHundred thousands:3 +0=3.\n\nTen thousands:0 +1=1 plus carry 1? Wait, earlier steps. Wait, in step 5, ten thousands place: 0 (from first number) +1 (from second) + carry 1 (from thousands place) which was carried over. Wait, no. Let's go back..\n\nWait, let me retrace the steps carefully:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\n1. Ones: 0 +8=8. Sum digit 8. Carry 0..\n\n2. Tens:0 +1=1. Sum digit 1. Carry 0..\n\n3. Hundreds:4 +8=12. Sum digit 2. Carry 1..\n\n4. Thousands:8 +1=9, plus carry 1=10. Sum digit 0. Carry 1..\n\n5. Ten thousands:0 