4 +1=5 →5, no carry..\n\nTen-thousands: 0 +8=8 →8, no carry..\n\nHundred-thousands:1 +9=10 →0, carry 1..\n\nMillions:3 +4 +1=8 →8, no carry..\n\nTen-millions:8 +4=12 →2, carry1..\n\nHundred-millions:4 +5 +1=10 →0, carry1..\n\nBut wait, after adding all digits, there's a carryover of 1 at the hundred millions place. So we need to add that as a new digit at the beginning..\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nStart from the ones place:.\n\nOnes:3.\n\nTens:4.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nTen-thousands:8.\n\nHundred-thousands:0 (with a carryover from previous).\n\nMillions:8.\n\nTen-millions:2 (from 8+4=12, write 2 carry 1).\n\nHundred-millions:0 (4+5=9, plus carry 1 makes 10, so write 0 carry1).\n\nThen the final carryover becomes a new digit:1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
