the thousands place. Wait, no, actually, when adding digit by digit from right to left, each step's carry is added to the next higher place. So after adding ones (12), carry 1 to tens. Then tens (8+4=12 +1=13, carry 1 to hundreds). Hundreds (9+6=15 +1=16, carry1 to thousands). So thousands place: 2 (from first number) +1 (from second number) =3, plus the carry 1 from hundreds: 3+1=4. So thousands place is 4, no carry..\n\nTen thousands place: 2 (first) +0 (second) =2, plus carry 0 → 2..\n\nHundred thousands place:5 (first) +0 (second) =5, no carry..\n\nMillions place:7 (first) +4 (second) =11. Wait, but millions place: first number has 7 in millions (since it's 967,522,983 → the millions digit is the third from the left, which is 7). Second number is 374,001,649 → millions digit is 4. So 7+4=11. So write down 1 and carry 1..\n\nTen millions place:6 (first) +7 (second) =13, plus the carried 1 →14. So write 4, carry 1..\n\nHundred millions place:9 +3=12, plus carried 1 →13. So write 13 here..\n\nPutting it all together from the highest place to lowest:.\n\nHundred millions:13.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:1 (from 7+4=11, which was written as 1 with carry 1).\n\nWait, no. Wait, let's list each digit after addition:.\n\nStart from the right:.\n\nOnes:2.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nHundred thousands:5.\n\nMillions:11 (but here, how does that translate? Wait, the millions place is the third digit from the left in each number. So when adding the millions digits (7 and4), we get 11. So we write 1 in the millions place and carry 1 to the ten millions place. Then ten millions place:6+7=13 plus the carried 1=14. So write 4 in ten millions, carry 1. Then hundred millions:9+3=12 plus 1=13. So the digits would be:.\n\nHundred millions:13.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:1.\n\nThen hundred thousands:5.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nThousands:4.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nTens:3.\n\nOnes:2.\n\nBut writing 13 in the hundred millions place would be 1 followed by