3 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 3 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones). .\n\nWait, when adding the ten-millions place: first number is 2, second is 3. So 2 + 3 = 5, plus any carry? Wait, earlier steps: hundred-thousands place was 8 + 3 +1 (carry) which was 12. So carry 1 to millions place. Then millions place: first number has 3, second has 0. 3 + 0 +1 (carry) =4. Wait, I think I made a mistake earlier. Let me redo the steps properly..\n\nLet me line up the numbers:.\n\n  623,832,096.\n+ 130,437,866.\n----------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nOnes: 6 + 6 = 12 → 2, carry 1..\nTens: 9 + 6 = 15 +1 = 16 → 6, carry 1..\nHundreds: 0 + 8 = 8 +1 = 9 → 9, carry 0..\nThousands: 2 +7 =9 → 9, carry 0..\nTen-thousands:3 +3 =6 →6, carry 0..\nHundred-thousands:8 +4=12 →2, carry1..\nMillions:3 +0=3 +1=4 →4, carry0..\nTen-millions:2 +3=5 →5, carry0..\nHundred-millions:6 +1=7 →7</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
