igit is 7 (since 457,228,733 → 457 million), and the second number is 874 million, which has 4 in the millions place? Wait, no. Wait, 874,687,978: breaking down, the digits are:.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nTen millions:7.\n\nMillions:4.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:8.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nTens:7.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nSo millions digit is 4. The first number is 457,228,733, so millions digit is 7. So adding millions place:7 +4=11. So write 1, carryover 1..\n\nThen ten millions place:5 (from first number) +7 (from second) =12, plus carryover 1 →13. So digit is 3, carryover 1..\n\nHundred millions place:4 (from first number) +8 (from second) =12, plus carryover 1 →13. So digit is 3, carryover 1. Since there are no higher places, that carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the left, making it 13 in the hundred millions place? Wait, but the hundred millions place is already 12 +1=13, so we write 3 and carryover 1. But since there's no higher place, we add that 1 as a new digit. So the total becomes 1 (billion place) then 3 (hundred million), etc..\n\nSo putting all together:.\n\nStart from the highest digit:.\n\nThe carryover 1 becomes the billions place:1.\n\nThen hundred millions:3.\n\nTen millions:3.\n\nMillions:1.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nTens:1.\n\nOnes:1.\n\nWait, wait, let me verify again step by step..\n\nLet me write each digit position:.\n\nNumber1: 457,228,733 → digits from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\nOnes:3.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nTen thousands:2.\n\nHundred thousands:2.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nTen millions:5.\n\nHundred millions:4.\n\nNumber2:874,687,978 → digits:.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nTens:7.\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nThousands:7.\n\nTen thousands:8.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nMillions:4.\n\nTen millions:7.\n\nHundred millions:8.\n\nAdding each digit from right to left with carryover:.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 3 +8 =11 → sum digit 1, carryover 1..\n\nPosition 2 (tens):3 +7 +1=