ch step properly:.\n\nStarting from the right (ones) to the left (hundred-millions):.\n\n1. Ones: 7+7=14 → 4, carry 1..\n2. Tens: 5+6=11 +1=12 → 2, carry 1..\n3. Hundreds: 1+9=10 +1=11 →1, carry 1..\n4. Thousands: 3+4=7 +1=8 →8, no carry..\n5. Ten-thousands: 7+6=13 →3, carry 1..\n6. Hundred-thousands: 4+6=10 +1=11 →1, carry 1..\n7. Millions: 4+5=9 +1=10 →0, carry 1..\n8. Ten-millions:7+7=14 +1=15 →5, carry 1..\n9. Hundred-millions:8+7=15 +1=16 →6, carry 1. Wait, but the hundred-millions place addition would be 8 (from first number) +7 (from second number) which is 15, plus the carried 1 makes 16. But since there's no higher place, we just write 16 here. So the final digits would be 1 followed by 6, then the rest. Wait, but when adding the hundred-millions place, the sum is 16. So that would make the first digits 1 (as a new digit) followed by 6, then the next digits. Wait, that can't be right. Because 8 +7 =15, plus the carryover 1 from the ten-millions place, which was 1. Wait, let me check again..\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the carryover from the ten-millions place. Let me go through each step again carefully:.\n\nLet me write the numbers vertically:.\n\n          8 7 4 4 7 3 1 5 7.\n        + 7 7 5 6 6 4 9 6 7.\n        -------------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 7 +7 =14 → write 4, carry 1..\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 5 +6 =11 +1 (carry) =12 → write 2, carry 1..\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):1 +9=10 +1=11 → write 1, carry 1..\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):3 +4=7 +1=8 → write 8, carry 0..\n\nPosition 5 (ten-thousands):7 +6=13 → write 3, carry 1..\n\nPosition 6 (hundred-thousands):4 +6=10 +1=11 → write 1, carry 1..\n\nPosition 7 (millions):4 +5=9 +1=10 → write 0, carry 1..\n\nPosition 8 (ten-millions):7 +7=14 +1=15 → write 5, carry 1..\n\nPosition 9 (hundred-millions):8 +7=15 +1=16 → write 6, carry 1..\n\nWait, but after adding the hundred-millions place (position 9), we have a carryover of 1, but there are no more digits left. So that carryover becomes a new digit at the beginning. So the final sum would be 1 followed by 6 (from 16), then 5, 0, 1, 3, 8, 1, 2, 4</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 65%|######5   | 326/500 [16:30<09:28,  3.27s/it] 65%|######5   | 327/500 [16:33<08:49,  3.06s/it]
