nds:9.\nTen thousands:5.\nThousands:3.\nHundreds:9.\nTens:3.\nOnes:5.\n\nSecond:704,882,290 →7 0 4, 8 8 2, 2 9 0..\n\nHundred millions:7.\nTen millions:0.\nMillions:4.\nHundred thousands:8.\nTen thousands:8.\nThousands:2.\nHundreds:2.\nTens:9.\nOnes:0.\n\nNow, adding each position starting from the ones:.\n\nOnes:5 + 0 = 5. So ones digit is 5..\n\nTens:3 +9 =12. So tens digit is 2, carryover 1..\n\nHundreds:9 +2 =11, plus the carryover 1 is 12. So hundreds digit 2, carryover 1..\n\nThousands:3 +2 =5, plus 1 →6. Thousands digit 6. No carryover..\n\nTen thousands:5 +8 =13. Ten thousands digit 3, carryover 1..\n\nHundred thousands:9 +8 =17, plus 1 →18. Hundred thousands digit 8, carryover 1..\n\nMillions:0 +4 =4, plus 1 →5. Millions digit 5. No carryover..\n\nTen millions:7 +0 =7. Ten millions digit 7..\n\nHundred millions:9 +7 =16. Hundred millions digit 6, carryover 1. But wait, there are no higher places, so that carryover 1 would be a new digit at the billions place..\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nTens:2.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nHundred thousands:8.\n\nMillions:5.\n\nTen millions:7.\n\nHundred millions:6 (from 9 +7 =16, write 6, carryover 1).\n\nBut then the carryover 1 adds to a new digit: billions place, which is 1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 66%|######5   | 329/500 [16:38<08:06,  2.85s/it] 66%|######6   | 330/500 [16:40<07:49,  2.76s/it]
