messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 649239260 and 698773125?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let's see. I need to add 649,239,260 and 698,773,125. Hmm, starting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. So 0 + 5 is 5. That's straightforward..\n\nNext, the tens place: 6 + 2. Wait, wait. Wait, let me write down the numbers properly to avoid confusion. Let's align them:.\n\n649,239,260.\n+.\n698,773,125.\n--------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes place: 0 + 5 = 5. So ones digit is 5..\n\nTens place: 6 (from 649...260) + 2 (from 698...125) = 8. Tens digit is 8..\n\nHundreds place: 2 (from first number) + 1 (second number) = 3. Hundreds digit 3..\n\nThousands place: 9 + 7. Wait, 9 +7 is 16. So we write down 6 and carry over 1..\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 (from first number) + 3 (from second) plus the carryover 1. 3+3+1=7. So 7 here..\n\nHundred-thousands place: 2 (first number) + 7 (second). 2+7=9. No carryover..\n\nMillions place: 9 (from first) + 8 (from second). 9+8=17. So write 7, carry over 1..\n\nTen-millions place: 4 (first) +9 (second) plus 1 carried over. 4+9=13 +1=14. So 4 here, carry over 1..\n\nHundred-millions place: 6 (first) +6 (second) +1 carried. 6+6=12 +1=13. So 3 here, carry over 1. Wait, but wait, are these the correct digits? Let me check the original numbers again..\n\nWait, the first number is 649,239,260. Breaking it down:.\n\nDigits from right to left:.\n\n0 (ones).\n6 (tens).\n2 (hundreds).\n9 (thousands).\n3 (ten thousands).\n2 (hundred thousands).\n9 (millions).\n4 (ten millions).\n6 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 698,773,125.\n\nDigits from right:.\n\n5 (ones).\n2 (tens).\n1 (hundreds).\n3 (thousands).\n7 (ten thousands).\n7 (hundred thousands).\n8 (millions).\n9 (ten millions).\n6 (hundred millions).\n\nSo aligning each place:.\n\nOnes: 0 +5=5.\nTens:6 +2=8.\nHundreds:2 +1=3.\nThousands:9 +3=12 (write 2, carry 1).\nTen thousands:3 +7=10 plus carry 1=11 (write 1, carry 1).\nHundred thousands:2 +7=9 plus carry 0=9.\nMillions:9 +8=17 (write 7, carry 1).\nTen millions:4 +9=13 plus carry 1=14 (write 4, carry 1).\nHundred millions:6 +6=12 plus carry 1=13 (write 3, carry 1).\nBut then, since there are no more digits beyond hundred millions, the carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the billions place. So the final sum would be 1,3 (from hundred millions) then the rest. So putting it all together:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nTens:8.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:2 (with a carryover 1).\n\nTen thousands:1 (with carryover 1).\n\nHundred thousands:9 (no carryover).\n\nMillions:7 (carryover 1).\n\nTen millions:4 (carryover 1).\n\nHundred millions:3 (carryover 1).\n\nThen billions:1..\n\nSo combining all digits from left to right:.\n\n1 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 5 (ones). Wait, that can't be right. Let me check again..\n\nWait, when adding hundred millions place: 6 +6=12 plus carryover 1 is 13. So we write 3 there and carry over 1. Then the next digit is billions place, which is 1. So the full number would be 1,3 (from hundred millions), then the rest. Wait, let's reconstruct the sum step by step..\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nTens:8.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nThousands:9+3=12. So 2 in thousands, carry 1..\n\nTen thousands:3 (from first number's ten thousands place: 649,239,260 is 649 million, 239 thousand, 260. So 649,239,260 has 4 in the ten millions place, 9 in the millions, 2 in the hundred thousands, 3 in the ten thousands, 9 in thousands, 2 in hundreds, 6 in tens, 0 in ones. Wait, maybe I made a mistake in the digit positions. Let me break down each number properly..\n\nFirst number: 649,239,260.\n\nDigits (from right, starting at ones):.\n\nPosition: 1: 0.\n\n10:6.\n\n100:2.\n\n1,000:9.\n\n10,000:3.\n\n100,000:2.\n\n1,000,000:9.\n\n10,000,000:4.\n\n100,000,000:6.\n\nSecond number:698,773,125.\n\nDigits:.\n\n1:5.\n\n10:2.\n\n100:1.\n\n1,000:3.\n\n10,000:7.\n\n100,000:7.\n\n1,000,000:8.\n\n10,000,000:9.\n\n100,000,000:6.\n\nSo now adding each position:.\n\n1: 0 +5 =5.\n\n10:6 +2=8.\n\n100:2 +1=3.\n\n1,000:9 +3=12 → write 2, carry 1.\n\n10,000:3 +7=10 +1 (carry) →11 → write 1, carry 1.\n\n100,000:2 +7=9 +0 carry →9.\n\n1,000,000:9 +8=17 →7, carry 1.\n\n10,000,000:4 +9=13 +1 (carry) →14 →4, carry 1.\n\n100,000,000:6 +6=12 +1=13 →3, carry 1.\n\nNow, since there are no higher places, the carry 1 goes to the billions place..\n\nSo the sum is 1,3 (from 100,000,000), then 4 (10,000,000),7 (1,000,000),9 (100,000),1 (10,000),2 (1,000),3 (100),8 (10),5 (1)..\n\nPutting it all together: 1,347,912,385..\n\nWait, let me check:.\n\n1 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions),7 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),1 (ten thousands),2 (thousands),3 (hundreds),8 (tens),5 (ones). So 1,347,912,385. But wait, let me verify by adding the numbers directly..\n\n649,239,260 + 698,773,125..\n\nLet me compute this:.\n\n649,239,260.\n\n+698,773,125.\n\n= ?.\n\nAdding:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\n0+5=5.\n\n6+2=8.\n\n2+1=3.\n\n9+3=12 (carry 1).\n\n3+7=10 +1=11 (carry 1).\n\n2+7=9.\n\n9+8=17 (carry 1).\n\n4+9=13 +1=14 (carry 1).\n\n6+6=12 +1=13 (carry 1).\n\nThen the final carry 1..\n\nSo the sum is 1,347,012,385? Wait, wait, maybe I messed up the digits in the middle. Wait, when we added the 10,000 place: 3 +7 +1 (carry) =11, so 1 written there. Then the hundred thousands place: 2 +7 =9. Then millions place:9 +8=17. Ten millions:4+9+1=14. Hundred millions:6+6+1=13. Then the billions place:1..\n\nSo the digits would be:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:3.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:7.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nTen thousands:1.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nHundreds:3.\n\nTens:8.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nSo the number is 1,347,912,385. Let me check with another method. Let's add 649,239,260 + 698,773,125..\n\nAlternatively, 649 million + 698 million is 1,347 million. Then the rest: 239,260 +773,125. Wait, 239,260 +773,125. Let's compute that: 239,260 +700,000=939,260, then 73,125: 939,260 +73,125=1,012,385</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 67%|######7   | 336/500 [16:59<09:17,  3.40s/it]
