usands).\n4 (hundreds).\n1 (tens).\n4 (ones).\n\nSo adding digit by digit:.\n\nOnes: 6 +4 =10 → 0, carry 1..\n\nTens:4 +1=5 +1=6..\n\nHundreds:3 +4=7..\n\nThousands:4 +1=5..\n\nTen thousands:1 +6=7..\n\nHundred thousands:9 +0=9..\n\nMillions:4 +7=11 →1, carry 1..\n\nTen millions:3 +1=4 +1 (carry)=5..\n\nHundred millions:3 +9=12. So here, write 2 and carry 1, but since there are no higher digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning..\n\nSo putting it all together:.\n\nFrom right to left:.\n\nOnes:0.\n\nTens:6.\n\nHundreds:7.\n\nThousands:5.\n\nTen thousands:7.\n\nHundred thousands:9.\n\nMillions:1 (from 11) with a carryover 1..\n\nTen millions:5 (from 3+1+1).\n\nHundred millions:12 (3+9), so write 2 and carry 1..\n\nThen the final carryover 1 becomes the billions place:1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
