s), 2 (tens), 3 (ones). Wait, that gives 980,044,823? Let me verify each step again to make sure I didn't make a mistake..\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me write each digit position properly:.\n\nLet's break down both numbers into their digits:.\n\n121,876,445:.\n- Hundred millions: 1.\n- Ten millions: 2.\n- Millions: 1.\n- Hundred thousands: 8.\n- Ten thousands: 7.\n- Thousands: 6.\n- Hundreds: 4.\n- Tens: 4.\n- Ones: 5.\n\n967,866,178:.\n- Hundred millions: 9.\n- Ten millions: 6.\n- Millions: 7.\n- Hundred thousands: 8.\n- Ten thousands: 6.\n- Thousands: 6.\n- Hundreds: 1.\n- Tens: 7.\n- Ones: 8.\n\nAdding each position from right to left:.\n\nOnes: 5 +8=13 → 3, carry 1..\nTens: 4 +7=11 +1=12 → 2, carry 1..\nHundreds:4 +1=5 +1=6? Wait, wait, the first number's hundreds digit is 4 and the second's is 1. So 4+1=5, plus carryover 1 is 6. So hundreds place is 6. Wait, I thought earlier I wrote 8 here. That's a mistake. Oops! Let me correct that..\n\nSo I must have made an error in my initial calculation. Let me redo it properly step by step..\n\nStarting over:.\n\n1. Ones place: 5 +8 =13 → 3, carry 1..\n2. Tens place: 4 +7=11 +1=12 → 2, carry 1..\n3. Hundreds place:4 +1=5 +1=6 → 6, carry 0..\n4. Thousands place:6 +6=12 → 2, carry 1..\n5. Ten thousands place:7 +6=13 +1=14 →4, carry1..\n6. Hundred thousands place:8 +8=16 +1=17 →7, carry1..\n7. Millions place:1 +7=8 +1=9 →9, carry0..\n8. Ten millions place:2 +6=8 →8, carry0..\n9. Hundred millions place:1 +9=10 →0, carry1. Wait, but here, after adding the hundred millions digits (1 and 9), we get 10. So write 0 here and carry over 1. But since there are no higher places, that carryover becomes a new digit at the beginning. So the total would be 1,0 (hundred millions), then the rest..\n\nWait, that changes things. Let me re-express:.\n\nAfter adding each digit:.\n\nOnes:3.\nTens:2.\nHundreds:6.\nThousands:2 (from 6+6=12, carry 1).\nTen thousands:4 (7+6=13, plus 1 carried =14, so 4 carry1).\nHundred thousands:7