 4 (hundred thousands).\n- 0 (ten thousands).\n- 9 (thousands).\n- 8 (hundreds).\n- 1 (tens).\n- 8 (ones).\n\nWait, when adding, each position should be:.\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\n8 +8 =16 (ones).\n6 +1 +1=8 (tens).\n0 +8=8 (hundreds).\n9 +9=18 (thousands).\n2 +0 +1=3 (ten thousands).\n2 +4=6 (hundred thousands).\n4 +9=13 (millions).\n1 +7 +1=9 (ten millions).\n3 +6=9 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, let me check again step by step to avoid mistakes..\n\nLet's align them:.\n\n314,229,068.\n+679,409,818.\n=?.\n\nBreaking each digit by position:.\n\nHundred millions place: 3 +6 =9.\nTen millions place:1 +7=8.\nMillions place:4 +9=13 (write 3, carry 1).\nHundred thousands place:2 +4=6 (plus carry 1? Wait, no, the carry from millions would affect the next higher place, which is ten millions? Wait, no, when adding the millions place digits (4 and 9), the sum is 13. So we write 3 in the millions place and carry 1 to the ten millions place. But the ten millions digits are 1 and 7. So 1+7=8 plus the carried 1 makes 9 in ten millions. Then hundred millions is 3+6=9..\n\nWait, maybe I confused the places earlier. Let me redo the addition step by step, digit by digit, from right to left..\n\nOnes place: 8 +8 =16. Record 6, carry 1..\n\nTens place: 6 (from 314,229,068) +1 (from 679,409,818) =7. Plus the carry 1 makes 8. Record 8, no carry..\n\nHundreds place:0 +8 =8. Plus no carry. Record 8..\n\nThousands place:9 +9=18. Record 8, carry 1..\n\nTen-thousands place:2 +0=2. Plus carry 1=3. Record 3..\n\nHundred-thousands place:2 +4=6. Record 6..\n\nMillions place:4 +9=13. Record 3, carry 1..\n\nTen-millions place:1 +7=8. Plus carry 1=9. Record 9..\n\nHundred-millions place:3 +6=9. Record 9..\n\nSo putting it all together: the digits from each place are:.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nTen millions:9.\n\nMillions:3.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:3.\n\nThousands:8.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nTens:8.\n\nOnes:6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
