messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 718309891 and 962628624?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let's see. I need to add 718,309,891 and 962,628,624. Hmm, both numbers are pretty big, so I should line them up by place value and add each column starting from the ones place. Let me write them down:.\n\n718,309,891.\n+962,628,624.\n-------------.\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones place): 1 + 4 = 5. So the ones place of the sum is 5..\n\nNext is the tens place: 9 + 2 = 11. Wait, 9 (from the first number's tens place) plus 2 (from the second number's tens place) equals 11. So I write down 1 here and carry over 1 to the next column..\n\nHundreds place: 8 + 6 = 14, plus the carried 1 makes 15. So the hundreds digit is 5, carry over 1..\n\nThousands place: 1 (from first number) + 8 (from second) = 9, plus the carry 1 makes 10. Write 0, carry 1..\n\nTen-thousands place: 9 + 2 = 11, plus 1 is 12. Write 2, carry 1..\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 6 = 6, plus 1 is 7. No carry here..\n\nMillions place: 8 + 8 = 16. Write 6, carry 1..\n\nTen-millions place: 1 + 6 = 7, plus 1 carried makes 8..\n\nHundred-millions place: 7 + 9 = 16. So that's 6 with a carry 1, but since there are no more digits, we add the carry to the front. Wait, actually, let me check the places again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits..\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the places. Let me write both numbers aligned properly:.\n\n       7 1 8 3 0 9 8 9 1.\n    + 9 6 2 6 2 8 6 2 4.\n    -------------------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes: 1 +4=5.\nTens:9 +2=11 (1, carry 1).\nHundreds:8 +6=14 +1=15 (5, carry1).\nThousands:9 +8=17 +1=18? Wait, wait, wait. Wait, the thousands place. Let me check the original numbers again. The first number is 718,309,891. Breaking it down:.\n\nDigits (from right to left, ones to highest place):.\n\n1 (ones).\n9 (tens).\n8 (hundreds).\n9 (thousands).\n0 (ten thousands).\n3 (hundred thousands).\n8 (millions).\n1 (ten millions).\n7 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 962,628,624.\n\nDigits:.\n\n4 (ones).\n2 (tens).\n6 (hundreds).\n8 (thousands).\n2 (ten thousands).\n6 (hundred thousands).\n2 (millions).\n6 (ten millions).\n9 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, so when aligning:.\n\nFirst number: 7 1 8 3 0 9 8 9 1.\n\nSecond number:9 6 2 6 2 8 6 2 4.\n\nSo each digit from right to left (ones to hundred millions):.\n\n1st number: 1 (ones), 9 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 9 (thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 3 (hundred thousands), 8 (millions), 1 (ten millions), 7 (hundred millions).\n\n2nd number:4 (ones), 2 (tens),6 (hundreds),8 (thousands),2 (ten thousands),6 (hundred thousands),8 (millions),6 (ten millions),9 (hundred millions).\n\nNow, adding each column:.\n\nOnes:1+4=5 → sum digit 5, carry 0.\n\nTens:9+2=11 → sum digit 1, carry 1.\n\nHundreds:8+6=14 + carry 1=15 → sum digit 5, carry1.\n\nThousands:9+8=17 +1=18 → sum 8, carry 1.\n\nTen thousands:0+2=2 +1=3 → sum 3, carry 0.\n\nHundred thousands:3+6=9 +0=9 → sum9, carry0.\n\nMillions:8+8=16 → sum6, carry1.\n\nTen millions:1+6=7 +1=8 → sum8, carry0.\n\nHundred millions:7+9=16 → sum6, carry1.\n\nBut since there are no higher places, the carry 1 becomes a new digit at the front. So putting it all together:.\n\nFrom the highest place to the lowest:.\n\nCarry 1, then 6 (hundred millions), 8 (ten millions),6 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),3 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),5 (hundreds),1 (tens),5 (ones)..\n\nWait, but wait, let me recheck:.\n\nWait, after adding the hundred millions place: 7 (from first number) +9 (second) =16, so write 6, carry1. Then since there are no more digits beyond hundred millions, we add the carry 1 as a new digit at the beginning. So the total sum would be 1,6 (from hundred millions), then the rest..\n\nSo combining all digits:.\n\n1 (from carry) 6 (hundred millions), then 8 (ten millions), 6 (millions),9 (hundred thousands),3 (ten thousands),8 (thousands),5 (hundreds),1 (tens),5 (ones). So the sum is 1,686,938,515..\n\nWait, let me check again:.\n\nLet me compute step by step with the actual numbers:.\n\n718,309,891.\n\n+962,628,624.\n\n= ?.\n\nLet me add them as numbers:.\n\n718,309,891 + 962,628,624.\n\n= (700,000,000 + 962,628,624) + 18,309,891.\n\n= 1,662,628,624 + 18,309,891.\n\n= 1,662,628,624 + 10,000,000 = 1,672,628,624</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 72%|#######1  | 358/500 [18:02<07:36,  3.21s/it]
