arts with 12... Wait, let me check again..\n\nWait, when adding the hundred-millions place: the first number is 4 (since it's 460 million) and the second is 7 (767 million). 4 +7 =11, plus the carried 1 from the previous step (from ten-millions place) which was 1. So 11 +1 =12. So write down 2 and carry over 1. But since there are no higher digits, that carry-over 1 becomes the next digit. So the sum should be 1,2... etc</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
