s 10. So write 0 and carry over 1..\n\nHundred-millions place: 6 (from first) plus 2 (from second) plus the carried 1. 6+2=8, plus 1 is 9. So that's 9 here. No carry-over left..\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right, the digits are 6 (ones), 9 (tens), 9 (hundreds), 9 (thousands), 7 (ten-thousands), 1 (hundred-thousands), 1 (millions), 0 (ten-millions), 9 (hundred-millions)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
