ly is crucial. Let me write them out properly:.\n\n  269,540,554  .\n+ 152,139,612  .\n= ?.\n\nStarting from the right (ones):.\n\nOnes: 4 + 2 = 6  .\nTens: 5 + 1 = 6  .\nHundreds: 5 + 6 = 11 (write 1, carry 1)  .\nThousands: 0 + 9 = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10 (write 0, carry 1)  .\nTen-thousands: 4 + 3 = 7 + 1 = 8  .\nHundred-thousands: 5 + 1 = 6  .\nMillions: 9 + 2 = 11 (write 1, carry 1)  .\nTen-millions: 6 + 5 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12 (write 2, carry 1)  .\nHundred-millions: 2 + 1 = 3 + 1 (carry) = 4..\n\nWait, that makes sense. Let me verify each step again to be sure..\n\nStarting from the ones place:.\n\n1. Ones: 4 (from first number) + 2 (second) = 6. Correct..\n\n2. Tens: 5 + 1 = 6. Correct..\n\n3. Hundreds: 5 + 6 = 11. So 1 written, carryover 1..\n\n4. Thousands: 0 + 9 = 9 + 1 (carry) = 10. So 0 here, carryover 1..\n\n5. Ten-thousands: 4 (from first number) + 3 (second) = 7 + 1 carry = 8. Right..\n\n6. Hundred-thousands: 5 (first) + 1 (second) = 6. No carry..\n\n7. Millions place: 9 (first) + 2 (second) = 11. Write 1, carryover 1..\n\n8. Ten-millions: 6 (first) +5 (second) = 11 +1 (carry) =12. Write 2, carryover 1..\n\n9. Hundred-millions: 2 (first) +1 (second) =3 +1 carry =4..\n\nPutting all together: 4 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 1 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones). Wait, no. Wait, let's arrange the digits properly. Let me list the digits from highest place to lowest:.\n\nHundred-millions: 4  .\nTen-millions: 2  .\nMillions: 1  .\nHundred-thousands:6  .\nTen-thousands:8  .\nThousands:0  .\nHundreds:1  .\nTens:6  .\nOnes:6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
