should write them out with place markers:.\n\n681,299,830:.\n- Hundred millions: 6.\n- Ten millions: 8.\n- Millions: 1.\n- Hundred thousands: 2.\n- Ten thousands:9.\n- Thousands:9.\n- Hundreds:8.\n- Tens:3.\n- Ones:0.\n\n571,800,877:.\n- Hundred millions:5.\n- Ten millions:7.\n- Millions:1.\n- Hundred thousands:8.\n- Ten thousands:0.\n- Thousands:0.\n- Hundreds:8.\n- Tens:7.\n- Ones:7.\n\nSo when adding each corresponding place:.\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\n0 +7 =7 (ones).\n3 +7 =10 → write 0, carry 1 (tens).\n8 +8 +1 (carry) =17 → write7, carry1 (hundreds).\n9 +0 +1=10 → write0, carry1 (thousands).\n9 +0 +1=10 → write0, carry1 (ten thousands).\n2 +8 +1=11 → write1, carry1 (hundred thousands).\n1 +1 +1=3 → write3 (millions).\n8 +7=15 → write5, carry1 (ten millions).\n6 +5 +1=12 → write2, carry1 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, but after hundred millions, there's a carry-over of 1. So the next place is billions. So the total sum would be 1 (billions), 2 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), etc..\n\nPutting it all together:.\n\nBillions place:1.\nHundred millions:2.\nTen millions:5.\nMillions:3.\nHundred thousands:1.\nTen thousands:0.\nThousands:0.\nHundreds:7.\nTens:0.\nOnes:7.\n\nWait, let me check again step by step..\n\nOnes place: 0 +7 =7 → ones digit 7, no carry..\n\nTens:3 +7 =10 → tens digit 0, carry 1..\n\nHundreds:8 +8 +1=17 → hundreds digit 7, carry 1..\n\nThousands:9 +0 +1=10 → thousands digit 0, carry1..\n\nTen thousands:9 +0 +1=10 → ten thousands 0, carry1..\n\nHundred thousands:2 +8 +1=11 → hundred thousands 1, carry1..\n\nMillions:1 (from first number) +1 (from second number?) Wait, the first number's millions place is 1, and the second number's millions place is 0 (since 571,800,877 is 571 million...). Wait, no. Let me check again..\n\nWait, the first number is 681,299,830. Breaking it down:.\n\n6 (hundred millions).\n8 (ten millions).\n1 (millions).\n2 (hundred thousands).\n9 (ten thousands).\n9 (thousands).\n8 (hundreds).\n3 (tens).\n0 (ones).\n\nSecond