3 = 6, plus carry 1 → 7.\nPosition 7 (millions): 7 + 4 = 11 → write 1, carry 1.\nPosition 8 (ten-millions): 3 + 3 = 6, plus carry 1 → 7.\nPosition 9 (hundred-millions): 7 + 2 = 9.\n\nWait, let me verify each position properly. Let's break down each number into individual digits:.\n\nFirst number: 737,315,520.\n\nDigits (from right to left, positions 1 to 9):.\n1: 0.\n2: 2.\n3: 5.\n4: 1.\n5: 5.\n6: 3.\n7: 7.\n8: 3.\n9: 7.\n\nSecond number: 234,356,261.\n\nDigits (from right to left):.\n1: 1.\n2: 6.\n3: 2.\n4: 6.\n5: 5.\n6: 3.\n7: 4.\n8: 3.\n9: 2.\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nPosition 1: 0 + 1 = 1 → sum digit 1, carry 0.\nPosition 2: 2 + 6 = 8 → sum digit 8, carry 0.\nPosition 3: 5 + 2 = 7 → sum digit 7, carry 0.\nPosition 4: 1 + 6 = 7 → sum digit 7, carry 0.\nPosition 5: 5 + 5 = 10 → sum digit 0, carry 1.\nPosition 6: 3 + 3 = 6 + carry 1 = 7 → sum digit 7, carry 0.\nPosition 7: 7 + 4 = 11 → sum digit 1, carry 1.\nPosition 8: 3 + 3 = 6 + carry 1 = 7 → sum digit 7, carry 0.\nPosition 9: 7 + 2 = 9 → sum digit 9, carry 0.\n\nPutting all the sum digits together from position 9 to 1: 9,7,7,1,7,0,7,8,1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
