\n\n368,502,912.\n331,062,010.\n\nOnes: 2 + 0 = 2.\nTens: 1 + 1 = 2.\nHundreds: 9 + 0 = 9.\nThousands: 2 + 0 = 2.\nTen-thousands: 0 + 6 = 6.\nHundred-thousands: 5 + 2 = 7.\nMillions: 8 + 1 = 9.\nTen-millions: 6 + 3 = 9.\nHundred-millions: 3 + 3 = 6.\n\nPutting all those digits together from left to right (hundred-millions to ones):.\n\n6 (hundred-millions).\n9 (ten-millions).\n9 (millions).\n7 (hundred-thousands).\n6 (ten-thousands).\n2 (thousands).\n9 (hundreds).\n2 (tens).\n2 (ones).\n\nSo the sum should be 699,762,922. Let me verify this with a calculator or another method. Alternatively, adding the numbers another way: 368,502,912 + 331,062,010. Let's break it down:.\n\n368,502,912 + 300,000,000 = 668,502,912</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
