 3 + 5 = 8.\nHundreds: 4 + 2 = 6.\nThousands: 2 + 4 = 6.\nTen thousands: 6 + 7 = 13 (carry 1).\nHundred thousands: 0 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 10 (carry 1 again).\nMillions: 3 + 4 + 1 (carry) = 8.\nTen millions: 6 + 4 = 10 (carry 1).\nHundred millions:5 +7 +1=13..\n\nWait, let me check again:.\n\nLet me write both numbers aligned:.\n\n563,062,438.\n744,974,250.\n-------------.\nAdding each digit starting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones: 8 + 0 = 8.\n2. Tens: 3 +5=8.\n3. Hundreds:4 +2=6.\n4. Thousands:2 +4=6.\n5. Ten thousands:6 +7=13. Write 3, carry 1..\n6. Hundred thousands:0 +9 +1 (carry) =10. Write 0, carry 1..\n7. Millions:3 +4 +1=8.\n8. Ten millions:6 +4=10. Write 0, carry 1..\n9. Hundred millions:5 +7 +1=13. Write 3, carry 1 (since this is the next place beyond hundred millions, which is billions)..\n10. Billions place: The carry-over 1 here</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
