e: 1 (from first number's thousands) + 3 (second number's thousands) = 4 + 1 (carry) = 5. No carry..\n\nTen-thousands place: 5 (first) + 2 (second) = 7. No carry..\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 (first) + 4 (second) = 4. No carry..\n\nMillions place: 9 (first) + 8 (second) = 17. So write 7, carry 1..\n\nTen-millions place: 9 (first) + 3 (second) = 12 + 1 (carry) = 13. Write 3, carry 1..\n\nHundred-millions place: 5 (first) + 7 (second) = 12 + 1 (carry) = 13. Write 3, carry 1..\n\nBut wait, we're at the hundred millions place, which is the highest digit here. So the carryover 1 becomes a new digit at the billions place. So putting it all together:</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
