o right: 1 (billion), 5 (hundred-million), 2 (ten-million), 9 (million), 7 (hundred-thousand), 4 (ten-thousand), 6 (thousand), 7 (hundred), 9 (ten), 0 (one). Wait, let me check that again..\n\nWait, let me verify each step to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let's go through each position again carefully..\n\nOnes: 5+5=10 → 0, carry 1..\n\nTens:5+3=8 +1=9 → 9, carry 0..\n\nHundreds:6+0=6 → 6, carry 0..\n\nThousands:4+3=7 →7, carry 0..\n\nTen-thousands:5+9=14 →4, carry 1..\n\nHundred-thousands:8+8=16 +1=17 →7, carry1..\n\nMillions:7+1=8 +1=9 →9, carry0..\n\nTen-millions:6+6=12 →2, carry1..\n\nHundred-millions:9+5=14 +1=15 →5, carry1..\n\nBillions:0+0=0 +1=1 →1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
