lion place: 5 (from 951 million) and 2 (from 721 million). 5 + 2 = 7. No carry here..\n\nHundred-million place: 9 (from first number's 951 million) and 7 (from second number's 721 million). Wait, wait. Wait, the first number is 951,189,292, which is 951 million. So the hundred-million place is 9. The second number is 721,703,633, so the hundred-million place is 7. 9 + 7 = 16. So write 6 in the hundred-million place and carry over 1 to the next place, which is the billions place..\n\nBillions place: Both numbers are under a billion, so originally there's nothing here. But we have a carry-over of 1, so that becomes 1 in the billions place..\n\nPutting all the digits together with the carries:.\n\nStarting from the right:.\n\nOnes:5.\n\nTens:2 (carry 1).\n\nHundreds:9.\n\nThousands:5 (carry 1).\n\nTen-thousands:2.\n\nHundred-thousands:2 (carry 1).\n\nMillions:9 (carry 1).\n\nTen-millions:7 (carry 0).\n\nHundred-millions:6 (carry 1).\n\nBillions:1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
