y-over 1=8. No carry-over..\n\nPosition6 (Hundred thousands):.\n\n2 +4=6, plus 0=6..\n\nPosition7 (Millions):.\n\n9 +9=18. Write 8, carry over 1..\n\nPosition8 (Ten millions):.\n\n1 +2=3, plus carry-over 1=4..\n\nPosition9 (Hundred millions):.\n\n5 +4=9..\n\nPutting it all together from position9 to position1:.\n\nHundred millions:9.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:8.\n\nThousands:0.\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nTens:7.\n\nOnes:3.\n\nWait, but wait, the thousands position had a sum of 10, so we wrote 0 and carried 1. Then the ten thousands was 7+0+1=8. Then hundred thousands 2+4=6. Then millions 9+9=18, so 8 carry 1. Ten millions 1+2+1=4. Hundred millions 5+4=9..\n\nSo combining the digits:.\n\nFrom left to right (hundred millions to ones):.\n\n9 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions), 8 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 3 (ones)</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 83%|########2 | 413/500 [20:48<03:48,  2.63s/it]
