messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the addition problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of <<number1>> and <<number2>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.\n1. The ones place: <<digit1>>\n2. The tens place: <<digit2>>\n<<other digits>>\nAnswer:\nTherefore, the final computed sum is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 976642949 and 374119888?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let's tackle adding 976,642,949 and 374,119,888. Hmm, starting from the rightmost digit, which is the ones place. So, 9 plus 8 is 17. I'll write down 7 and carry over 1..\n\nNext, the tens place: 4 plus 8 is 12, plus the carried 1 makes 13. Write 3, carry 1..\n\nMoving to the hundreds place: 9 plus 8 is 17, plus 1 is 18. That's 8 with a carry of 1..\n\nThousands place: 2 plus 9 is 11, plus 1 is 12. So 2 here, carry 1..\n\nTen-thousands place: 4 plus 1 is 5, plus 1 is 6. No carry-over here..\n\nHundred-thousands place: 6 plus 9 is 15. Write 5, carry 1..\n\nMillions place: 7 plus 4 is 11, plus 1 is 12. So 2, carry 1..\n\nTen-millions place: 6 plus 7 is 13, plus 1 is 14. That's 4, carry 1..\n\nFinally, the hundred-millions place: 9 plus 3 is 12, plus 1 is 13. So 13 here..\n\nPutting all those digits together: 1,3 (from hundred-millions), then 4, 2, 5, 6, 2, 8, 3, 7. Wait, let me check again. Maybe I messed up the order. Let me write each digit's place properly to avoid confusion. Starting from the right:.\n\nOnes:7.\n\nTens:3.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nThousands:2.\n\nTen-thousands:6.\n\nHundred-thousands:5.\n\nMillions:2.\n\nTen-millions:4</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
