llions place: First number is 8 (from 892,652,820) and the second is 5 (from 502,334,307). 8 + 5 = 13. So here we write down 3 and carry over 1 to the billions place..\n\nBillions place: The first number is 0 (since it's 892 million, so no higher digits) and the second is 0 as well. But we have the carried 1, so that becomes 1 in the billions place..\n\nPutting all those together: 1 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 4 (millions), 9 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 1 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 7 (ones). Wait, let me check the digits again to make sure I didn't mix up any places..\n\nWait, let me write the numbers aligned to ensure each digit is correctly placed:.\n\n       892,652,820.\n    + 502,334,307.\n    ----------------.\n    .\nStarting from the right:.\nOnes: 0 +7 =7.\nTens:2 +0=2.\nHundreds:8 +3=11 (write 1, carry 1).\nThousands:2 +4=6 +1=7.\nTen thousands:5 +3=8.\nHundred thousands:6 +3=9.\nMillions:2 +2=4.\nTen millions:9 +0=9.\nHundred millions:8 +5=13 (write 3, carry 1).\nBillions:0 +0 +1=1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
