om first number) and 0 (from second). 8 + 0 = 8. Ten-millions place is 8..\n\nThen the hundred-millions place: 2 (from first number) and 6 (from second). 2 + 6 = 8. So hundred-millions place is 8</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
