ce. Since both numbers are 9 digits, adding the carry-over 1 here. So that's 1 in the billions place..\n\nPutting all the digits together: 1 (billions), 8 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 7 (millions), 2 (hundred thousands), 4 (ten thousands), 4 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 3 (ones). Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix any digits. Let me go through each step once more to confirm..\n\nOnes: 2+1=3. Correct..\nTens: 4+4=8. Correct..\nHundreds:7+9=16, write 6, carry 1..\nThousands:5+8=13 +1=14, write 4, carry1..\nTen thousands:6+7=13 +1=14, write4, carry1..\nHundred thousands:4+7=11 +1=12, write2, carry1..\nMillions:9+7=16 +1=17, write7, carry1..\nTen millions:9+9=18 +1=19, write9, carry1..\nHundred millions:9+8=17 +1=18, write8, carry1..\nBillions: carry1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
