.\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands): 7 + 8 = 15 → 5, carry 1.\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands): 4 + 7 = 11 + 1 = 12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nPosition 7 (millions): 7 + 6 = 13 + 1 = 14 → 4, carry 1.\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions): 7 + 1 = 8 + 1 = 9 → 9, carry 0.\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions): 3 + 2 = 5 → 5..\n\nPutting it all together from right to left: 6, 3, 2, 9, 5, 2, 4, 9, 5..\n\nWait, let me check again step by step to make sure I didn't make a mistake in the positions..\n\nWait, perhaps breaking down each digit position:.\n\nFirst number: 377,477,256.\n\nDigits (from right to left):.\n\nPosition 1: 6 (ones).\n\nPosition 2: 5 (tens).\n\nPosition 3: 2 (hundreds).\n\nPosition 4: 7 (thousands).\n\nPosition 5: 7 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition 6: 4 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition 7: 7 (millions).\n\nPosition 8: 7 (ten millions).\n\nPosition 9: 3 (hundred millions).\n\nSecond number: 216,781,980.\n\nDigits (from right to left):.\n\nPosition 1: 0 (ones).\n\nPosition 2: 8 (tens).\n\nPosition 3: 9 (hundreds).\n\nPosition 4: 1 (thousands).\n\nPosition 5: 8 (ten thousands).\n\nPosition 6: 7 (hundred thousands).\n\nPosition 7: 6 (millions).\n\nPosition 8: 1 (ten millions).\n\nPosition 9: 2 (hundred millions).\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nPosition 1: 6 + 0 = 6.\n\nPosition 2: 5 + 8 = 13 → 3, carry 1.\n\nPosition 3: 2 + 9 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nPosition 4: 7 + 1 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9 → 9, carry 0.\n\nPosition 5: 7 + 8 = 15 → 5, carry 1.\n\nPosition 6: 4 + 7 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12 → 2, carry 1.\n\nPosition 7: 7 + 6 = 13 + 1 (carry) = 14 → 4, carry 1.\n\nPosition 8: 7 + 1 = 8 + 1 (carry) = 9 → 9, carry 0.\n\nPosition 9: 3 + 2 = 5 → 5</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
