ne). .\n\nWait, so when adding the ten-millions place: first number has 7 (ten million) and the second has 8 (ten million). So 7 + 8 = 15. So we write 5 in the ten-million place and carry over 1 to the hundred-million place..\n\nHundred-million place: 1 (from first number) + 1 (from second number) plus the carried 1. That's 1 +1 +1 =3. So 3 in the hundred-million place..\n\nPutting it all together, let's verify each step again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me write the addition step by step with carries:.\n\n          1 1 1.\n    1 7 3 6 0 9 4 8 7.\n  + 1 8 0 4 0 6 9 1 2.\n  ----------------------</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
