 wait, since these are the highest digits, we need to add that carry-over to the front. So the next place (billions place) would be 1..\n\nPutting all the digits together with the carries:.\n\nStart from the right:.\n\nOnes:7.\n\nTens:3 (carry 1).\n\nHundreds:2.\n\nThousands:6.\n\nTen-thousands:0 (carry 1).\n\nHundred-thousands:2 (carry 1).\n\nMillions:0 (carry 1).\n\nTen-millions:9.\n\nHundred-millions:6 (carry 1).\n\nThen the billions place:1</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
