s), 0 (hundred thousands), 6 (millions), 2 (ten millions), 4 (hundred millions).\n\n263,283,883: 3 (ones), 8 (tens), 8 (hundreds), 3 (thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 2 (hundred thousands), 3 (millions), 6 (ten millions), 2 (hundred millions).\n\nWait, maybe it's easier to align them:.\n\n       4 2 6 0 6 1 9 3 8.\n    + 2 6 3 2 8 3 8 8 3.\n    -------------------------.\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\n1. Ones place: 8 + 3 = 11. Write 1, carryover 1..\n2. Tens place: 3 + 8 = 11 + 1 (carry) = 12. Write 2, carryover 1..\n3. Hundreds place: 9 + 8 = 17 + 1 = 18. Write 8, carryover 1..\n4. Thousands place: 1 + 3 = 4 + 1 = 5. Write 5, no carryover..\n5. Ten thousands place: 6 + 8 = 14. Write 4, carryover 1..\n6. Hundred thousands place: 0 + 2 = 2 + 1 = 3. Write 3..\n7. Millions place: 6 + 3 = 9. Write 9..\n8. Ten millions place: 2 + 6 = 8. Write 8..\n9. Hundred millions place: 4 + 2 = 6. Write 6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
