write them vertically:.\n\n      5 2 4 0 1 8 5 1 1.\n    + 8 2 4 6 7 1 1 2 5.\n    -------------------.\nStarting from the right:.\n\n1. Ones place: 1 +5 =6 → no carry-over..\n2. Tens place:1 +2=3 → 3..\n3. Hundreds place:5 +1=6 →6..\n4. Thousands place:8 +1=9 →9..\n5. Ten-thousands place:1 +7=8 →8..\nWait, wait, maybe I messed up the places. Let me clarify the place values. Each digit from right is ones, tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, millions, ten millions, hundred millions..\n\nWait, let's list each position with their actual place names:.\n\nPosition (from right, starting at 1):.\n\n1: Ones.\n2: Tens.\n3: Hundreds.\n4: Thousands.\n5: Ten thousands.\n6: Hundred thousands.\n7: Millions.\n8: Ten millions.\n9: Hundred millions.\n\nSo the digits of the first number (524,018,511):.\n\nFrom right to left:.\nPosition 1 (ones):1.\nPosition 2 (tens):1.\nPosition 3 (hundreds):5.\nPosition 4 (thousands):8.\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):1.\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):0.\nPosition 7 (millions):4.\nPosition 8 (ten millions):2.\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):5.\n\nSecond number (824,671,125):.\n\nPosition 1:5.\nPosition 2:2.\nPosition 3:1.\nPosition 4:1.\nPosition 5:7.\nPosition 6:6.\nPosition 7:4.\nPosition 8:2.\nPosition 9:8.\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\nStarting from Position 1 (ones):.\n1 +5=6 → sum digit 6, carry 0..\n\nPosition 2 (tens):.\n1 +2=3 → sum digit 3, carry 0..\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):.\n5 +1=6 → sum digit 6, carry 0..\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):.\n8 +1=9 → sum digit 9, carry 0..\n\nPosition 5 (ten thousands):.\n1 +7=8 → sum digit 8, carry 0..\n\nPosition 6 (hundred thousands):.\n0 +6=6 → sum digit 6, carry 0..\n\nPosition 7 (millions):.\n4 +4=8 → sum digit 8, carry 0..\n\nPosition 8 (ten millions):.\n2 +2=4 → sum digit 4, carry 0..\n\nPosition 9 (hundred millions):.\n5 +8=13 → sum digit 3, carry 1..\n\nSince there's a carry of 1 after the hundred millions place, we add a new digit to the left (billions place):1..\n\nPutting all together, the sum is 1 (billions), 3 (hundred millions), 4 (ten millions),8 (millions),6 (hundred thousands),8 (ten thousands?), wait, let's reconstruct the digits in order from highest to lowest:.\n\nThe carry-over 1 is in the billions place..\n\nThen the hundred millions place is 3..\n\nThen ten millions:4.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:8.\n\nThousands:9.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nTens:3.\n\nOnes:6.\n\nWait, let me make sure the order is correct. The sum digits from left to right (highest to lowest place) would be:.\n\nBillions:1.\n\nHundred millions:3.\n\nTen millions:4.\n\nMillions:8.\n\nHundred thousands:6.\n\nTen thousands:8.\n\nThousands:9.\n\nHundreds:6.\n\nTens:3.\n\nOnes:6</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]] 94%|#########4| 471/500 [25:26<06:47, 14.04s/it]
