eds: 2 + 2 = 4.\nThousands: 5 + 6 = 11 (so write 1, carry over 1).\nTen-thousands: 6 (from first number) + 9 (from second) = 15, plus the carry-over 1 makes 16. So write 6, carry over 1..\nHundred-thousands: 7 (first) + 1 (second) = 8, plus carry 1 = 9. No carry-over here..\nMillions place: 5 (first) + 4 (second) = 9. No carry-over..\nTen-millions place: 8 (first) + 9 (second) = 17. Write 7, carry over 1..\nHundred-millions place: 2 (first) + 4 (second) = 6, plus carry 1 = 7..\n\nPutting it all together, starting from the right:.\n\nOnes:8.\nTens:9.\nHundreds:4.\nThousands:1 (with carry-over 1).\nTen-thousands:6 (carry-over 1).\nHundred-thousands:9.\nMillions:9.\nTen-millions:7 (carry-over 1).\nHundred-millions:7.\n\nWait, let me double-check each step to avoid mistakes..\n\nStarting from ones:.\n\n1. Ones: 6 + 2 = 8. Correct..\n2. Tens: 8 + 1 = 9. Correct..\n3. Hundreds: 2 + 2 = 4. Correct..\n4. Thousands: 5 (first number's thousands place) + 6 (second's thousands) = 11. So write 1, carry 1..\n5. Ten-thousands: 6 (first) + 9 (second) = 15, plus 1 carried = 16. So 6 here, carry 1..\n6. Hundred-thousands: 7 (first) +1 (second) =8, plus 1 carried =9. No carry..\n7. Millions:5 (first) +4 (second)=9. No carry..\n8. Ten-millions:8 (first) +9 (second)=17. Write 7, carry 1..\n9. Hundred-millions:2 +4=6, plus 1 carried=7</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
