 carry 1 makes 12. So 2 here, carry over 1..\n\nHundred-millions place: First number has 1 (from 174...), second has 2 (from 279...). 1 + 2 = 3, plus the carry 1 makes 4. So 4 here. No more digits beyond that..\n\nPutting all those digits together: starting from the right, the sum is 4 (hundred-millions), 2 (ten-millions), 6 (millions), 8 (hundred-thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), 1 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 4 (tens), 8 (ones). Wait, let me check again..\n\nWait, maybe I mixed up some steps. Let me recount the places carefully. Let's list each digit position step by step:.\n\nNumbers:.\n\n174,641,570.\n279,819,878.\n\nAligning them:.\n\n          1 7 4 6 4 1 5 7 0.\n        +2 7 9 8 1 9 8 7 8.\n        -------------------.\nStarting from the right (ones place):.\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 0 + 8 = 8. Sum digit 8. Carry 0..\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 7 + 7 = 14. Sum digit 4. Carry 1..\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds): 5 + 8 = 13. Plus carry 1 =14. Sum digit 4. Carry 1..\n\nPosition 4 (thousands):1 +9 =10. Plus carry 1=11. Sum digit 1. Carry 1..\n\nPosition 5 (ten-thousands):4 +8=12. Plus carry 1=13. Sum digit 3. Carry 1..\n\nPosition 6 (hundred-thousands):6 +1=7. Plus carry 1=8. Sum digit 8. Carry 0..\n\nPosition 7 (millions):4 +9=13. Sum digit 3. Carry 1. Wait, wait. Wait, the first number is 174,641,570. Breaking it down:.\n\nDigits:.\n\nHundred-millions: 1.\n\nTen-millions:7.\n\nMillions:4.\n\nHundred-thousands:6.\n\nTen-thousands:4.\n\nThousands:1.\n\nHundreds:5.\n\nTens:7.\n\nOnes:0.\n\nSimilarly, the second number 279,819,878:.\n\nHundred-millions:2.\n\nTen-millions:7.\n\nMillions:9.\n\nHundred-thousands:8.\n\nTen-thousands:1.\n\nThousands:9.\n\nHundreds:8.\n\nTens:7.\n\nOnes:8.\n\nSo when adding:.\n\nHundred-millions:1 +2 =3. But wait, after the millions place, there's a carry-over. Let me re-examine:.\n\nStarting from the right, as before:.\n\nOnes: 0+8=8, sum 8, carry 0..\n\nTens:7+7=14, sum 4, carry 1..\n\nHundreds:5+8=13, sum 4, carry 1..\n\nThousands:1+9=10, sum 0, carry 1. Wait, wait! Wait, here's a mistake. Earlier I thought the thousands place was 1 +9=10, but the first number's thousands digit is 1 (from 174,641,570: ...1 (thousands)), and the second number's thousands digit is 9 (from ...9 (thousands) in 279,819,878). So 1 +9=10. Sum digit is 0, carry 1. Oh! So I made a mistake here earlier. So the thousands place is 0 with a carry-over of 1..\n\nThen, ten-thousands place:4 (from first number) +1 (from second number). Wait, the ten-thousands digits: first number is 4 (since 174,641,570 is 1 (hundred-millions),7 (ten-millions),4 (millions),6 (hundred-thousands),4 (ten-thousands),1 (thousands)...). The second number's ten-thousands digit is 1 (279,819,878: ...1 (ten-thousands)). So 4 +1=5. Plus the carry-over 1 makes 6. So sum digit 6, carry 0. Wait, that's different from my previous calculation. Wait, this seems conflicting. Let's clarify..\n\nWait, let's break down each number into digits:.\n\nFirst number: 174,641,570.\n\nDigits (from right to left, but we'll write positions as per place value):.\n\n- Ones:0.\n\n- Tens:7.\n\n- Hundreds:5.\n\n- Thousands:1.\n\n- Ten-thousands:4.\n\n- Hundred-thousands:6.\n\n- Millions:4.\n\n- Ten-millions:7.\n\n- Hundred-millions:1.\n\nSecond number:279,819,878.\n\nDigits:.\n\n- Ones:8.\n\n- Tens:7.\n\n- Hundreds:8.\n\n- Thousands:9.\n\n- Ten-thousands:1.\n\n- Hundred-thousands:8.\n\n- Millions:9.\n\n- Ten-millions:7.\n\n- Hundred-millions:2.\n\nNow adding each position:.\n\n1. Ones:0 +8=8. Sum 8, carry 0..\n\n2. Tens:7 +7=14. Sum 4, carry 1..\n\n3. Hundreds:5 +8=13. Sum 3, carry 1. Wait, wait, 5+8=13, so sum digit 3, carry 1. Wait, I think I made a mistake here earlier. Previously I thought it was 4, but no, 5+8=13. So sum digit 3, carry 1. So here's another error..\n\nThen, thousands place:1 (from first number) +9 (from second) =10. Plus carry 1 is 11. Wait, no, carry from hundreds place is 1. So 1 +9=10, plus 1 is 11. So sum digit 1, carry 1. Wait, no. Wait, thousands place: 1 +9 =10. Add carry 